1
00:00:34,501 --> 00:00:35,711
Babe, what are you doing?

2
00:00:35,794 --> 00:00:37,504
I'm looking for the aloe iodine.

3
00:00:38,464 --> 00:00:39,465
It's not here.

4
00:00:39,548 --> 00:00:41,425
Yeah, because that's not where it is.

5
00:00:43,761 --> 00:00:46,680
Babe, can you give me 12 seconds
and I will come and get it for you?

6
00:00:46,764 --> 00:00:48,432
Twelve seconds is specific.

7
00:00:49,308 --> 00:00:50,976
Wow, these are very expired.

8
00:01:08,535 --> 00:01:10,954
Okay. Betadine. Chlorhexidine...

9
00:01:11,997 --> 00:01:12,998
No iodine.

10
00:01:14,875 --> 00:01:16,752
Right. Thanks.

11
00:01:29,056 --> 00:01:30,057
But...

12
00:01:30,849 --> 00:01:31,850
Well, that's not...

13
00:01:33,394 --> 00:01:34,645
We tried for two years.

14
00:01:34,728 --> 00:01:37,272
I know. I know, babe.

15
00:01:37,356 --> 00:01:39,274
I mean, we don't even
talk about it anymore.

16
00:01:39,358 --> 00:01:41,568
Talking was not the important part.

17
00:01:43,737 --> 00:01:46,490
It wasn't gonna be for us,
and we were okay with that.

18
00:01:46,573 --> 00:01:48,534
We were okay, but...

19
00:01:51,036 --> 00:01:52,079
Well...

20
00:01:55,207 --> 00:01:56,208
This is better.

21
00:01:57,209 --> 00:01:58,585
Yes. It's...

22
00:01:59,294 --> 00:02:00,587
It's a lot better, isn't it?

23
00:02:00,671 --> 00:02:01,672
This is great.

24
00:02:13,934 --> 00:02:16,645
Obviously, we're gonna need protocols
to account for our cell mutations...

25
00:02:16,728 --> 00:02:17,729
No, Reed.

26
00:02:17,813 --> 00:02:19,690
- ...monitoring for further cosmic effects.
- Reed.

27
00:02:20,441 --> 00:02:21,567
We can do this.

28
00:02:22,943 --> 00:02:24,361
Okay?

29
00:02:24,445 --> 00:02:25,946
I really want to do this.

30
00:02:26,029 --> 00:02:27,531
I really want to do this.

31
00:02:28,949 --> 00:02:29,950
Then what?

32
00:02:34,788 --> 00:02:36,832
Nothing is going to change.

33
00:02:38,250 --> 00:02:39,460
Of course not.

34
00:02:42,004 --> 00:02:44,715
<i>Ladies and gentlemen, we welcome you</i>

35
00:02:44,798 --> 00:02:50,304
<i>to a very special event celebrating
four years of the Fantastic Four.</i>

36
00:02:50,387 --> 00:02:54,057
<i>And now your host for the evening,
Ted Gilbert.</i>

37
00:02:54,141 --> 00:02:55,851
Well, now, folks.

38
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:59,021
Folks, we all know the story.

39
00:02:59,104 --> 00:03:03,901
Four brave astronauts head up into space,
encounter a bit of cosmic turbulence,

40
00:03:03,984 --> 00:03:05,486
and come back forever changed.

41
00:03:05,569 --> 00:03:09,781
Not just the molecules of their bodies
but also their place in our hearts.

42
00:03:10,407 --> 00:03:11,825
And, now, a look back.

43
00:03:11,909 --> 00:03:16,955
<i>This is </i>Excelsior<i> Launch Control.
T-minus 3 hours, 42 minutes, 19 seconds.</i>

44
00:03:17,039 --> 00:03:21,251
<i>Four years ago, man and woman conquered
the last frontier as we know it,</i>

45
00:03:22,044 --> 00:03:24,296
<i>the exploration of space.</i>

46
00:03:25,839 --> 00:03:27,633
The best pilot in the world, right here.

47
00:03:27,716 --> 00:03:29,593
Yeah. The best-looking he means.

48
00:03:32,679 --> 00:03:36,266
{\an8}<i>It was my mission, space exploration.</i>

49
00:03:36,350 --> 00:03:39,019
{\an8}<i>I assembled the best scientific minds
to come along,</i>

50
00:03:39,102 --> 00:03:44,816
<i>who also happened to be my best friend,
my wife and my brother-in-law.</i>

51
00:03:45,442 --> 00:03:47,444
Comms check. Everybody, sound off.

52
00:03:47,528 --> 00:03:49,196
- Check.
- Check, check.

53
00:03:49,279 --> 00:03:50,822
- Check.
- Comms are live.

54
00:03:51,448 --> 00:03:54,368
That last voice you just heard
was my baby brother, Jonathan Storm,

55
00:03:54,451 --> 00:03:56,912
and, ladies, he is very single.

56
00:03:58,789 --> 00:04:00,624
- Kiss for luck.
- Kiss?

57
00:04:03,210 --> 00:04:08,006
<i>However, Dr. Richards's expedition
encountered an unforeseen event</i>

58
00:04:08,090 --> 00:04:11,301
<i>that changed not only the lives
of these courageous individuals...</i>

59
00:04:11,385 --> 00:04:12,427
<i>Verify go for launch.</i>

60
00:04:12,511 --> 00:04:13,637
<i>Go for launch.</i>

61
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:16,056
<i>...but also the course of our history.</i>

62
00:04:16,139 --> 00:04:18,141
<i>- Come in, </i>Excelsior. <i>Come in,</i> Excelsior.
- <i>What is that?</i>

63
00:04:18,225 --> 00:04:19,518
<i>I don't know! I don't know!</i>

64
00:04:20,269 --> 00:04:22,437
<i>It must be the cosmic rays.</i>

65
00:04:22,521 --> 00:04:25,232
<i>- Ben! Ben!
- Ben!</i>

66
00:04:25,857 --> 00:04:28,569
Obviously, while we were in space
due to errors on my part...

67
00:04:28,652 --> 00:04:29,820
Stop.

68
00:04:29,903 --> 00:04:32,155
...we encountered a cosmic storm
that altered our DNA.

69
00:04:32,239 --> 00:04:35,242
<i>We came back with anomalies.</i>

70
00:04:37,995 --> 00:04:40,914
<i>And they returned with superpowers.</i>

71
00:04:51,717 --> 00:04:54,136
<i>They became our protectors.</i>

72
00:05:02,227 --> 00:05:03,437
Cannonball!

73
00:05:17,659 --> 00:05:19,620
<i>It's clobberin' time!</i>

74
00:05:44,853 --> 00:05:48,815
I was at the opening of the Pan Am Tower
when Mole Man attacked.

75
00:05:48,899 --> 00:05:52,527
<i>The Fantastic Four saved my life.</i>

76
00:06:04,748 --> 00:06:06,833
<i>Mole Man's attempt
to steal the Pan Am building</i>

77
00:06:06,917 --> 00:06:09,419
<i>was thwarted by the Fantastic Four.</i>

78
00:06:09,503 --> 00:06:14,091
This is all Reed Richards's fault.
Him and his endless pursuit of progress.

79
00:06:14,925 --> 00:06:16,468
Power to the underground!

80
00:06:20,263 --> 00:06:24,267
<i>And when the Mad Thinker
tried to sabotage New York City</i>

81
00:06:25,477 --> 00:06:28,730
<i>the Fantastic Four came to our rescue.</i>

82
00:06:29,981 --> 00:06:30,982
Gotcha!

83
00:06:34,695 --> 00:06:35,696
Have a great day!

84
00:06:38,281 --> 00:06:41,118
<i>They defeated Red Ghost
and his Super-Apes.</i>

85
00:06:52,379 --> 00:06:54,756
<i>They became our inspiration.</i>

86
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:58,677
This equation not only confirms
alternate dimensions,

87
00:06:58,760 --> 00:07:03,390
but it suggests parallel Earths exist
on different dimensional planes.

88
00:07:06,143 --> 00:07:07,644
Who wants to see a big explosion?

89
00:07:07,728 --> 00:07:08,979
Me!

90
00:07:10,605 --> 00:07:12,858
{\an8}<i>And they became our leaders.</i>

91
00:07:12,941 --> 00:07:17,112
<i>Sue Storm brokers peace deal
with Harvey "Mole Man" Elder,</i>

92
00:07:17,195 --> 00:07:20,198
<i>leader of the underground nation,
Subterranea.</i>

93
00:07:20,282 --> 00:07:22,951
<i>I don't trust surface dwellers.
I never have.</i>

94
00:07:23,034 --> 00:07:25,454
But I do trust Sue.

95
00:07:25,537 --> 00:07:31,209
We have come together today to form
a new charter, the Future Foundation.

96
00:07:31,293 --> 00:07:32,836
All participating countries

97
00:07:32,919 --> 00:07:35,881
agree to dismantle their armed forces.

98
00:07:35,964 --> 00:07:39,593
<i>And on this fourth anniversary
we celebrate them.</i>

99
00:07:39,676 --> 00:07:41,678
<i>They are the very best of us.</i>

100
00:07:41,762 --> 00:07:44,431
<i>They are the Fantastic Four.</i>

101
00:07:44,514 --> 00:07:47,809
Thank you, Fantastic Four!

102
00:07:47,893 --> 00:07:49,227
Thank you, Fantastic Four!

103
00:07:49,311 --> 00:07:51,354
- Thank you, Fantastic Four!
- We love you, Fantastic Four.

104
00:07:51,438 --> 00:07:53,064
- I love you, Johnny!
- Fantastic Four, we love you!

105
00:07:53,148 --> 00:07:56,777
- Thank you, Fantastic Four.
- Thank you, Fantastic Four.

106
00:07:58,236 --> 00:08:02,908
We are proud to call them our guides,
our protectors and our friends.

107
00:08:02,991 --> 00:08:06,495
Let's hear it for Reed, Sue,
Johnny and Ben.

108
00:08:14,795 --> 00:08:16,671
I must say,
that was all a bit aggrandizing.

109
00:08:16,755 --> 00:08:18,006
- Yeah.
- H.E.R.B.I.E.

110
00:08:18,089 --> 00:08:20,425
- H.E.R.B.I.E. with the herbs.
- How's that sauce looking?

111
00:08:21,218 --> 00:08:23,345
Don't do that.
Wash your hands first, please.

112
00:08:23,428 --> 00:08:25,222
- I was wearing my gloves the whole time.
- Just wash your hands.

113
00:08:25,305 --> 00:08:26,389
Let me try that.

114
00:08:29,059 --> 00:08:30,310
Okay.

115
00:08:31,311 --> 00:08:34,397
Okay. Is this guy good?

116
00:08:35,232 --> 00:08:36,817
That is fantastic.

117
00:08:37,526 --> 00:08:38,985
- Let me try.
- It's incredible stuff.

118
00:08:39,069 --> 00:08:40,153
Stop. Don't do that.

119
00:08:40,904 --> 00:08:42,739
Don't do that. It's not quite done.

120
00:08:42,823 --> 00:08:43,949
No, it's not quite done.

121
00:08:44,032 --> 00:08:46,910
No, it could be done,
but I'm gonna add a little more garlic.

122
00:08:46,993 --> 00:08:48,161
Not because it's not delicious.

123
00:08:48,245 --> 00:08:50,497
I just want to add
a little bit of zip, okay?

124
00:08:55,877 --> 00:08:56,878
What are you doing?

125
00:08:57,671 --> 00:08:59,047
What do you mean, what am I doing?

126
00:08:59,130 --> 00:09:01,591
- I mean, you're gonna ruin your appetite.
- I'm hungry.

127
00:09:05,345 --> 00:09:07,180
They're never late for Sunday dinner.

128
00:09:07,264 --> 00:09:08,765
Should we wait?

129
00:09:08,849 --> 00:09:09,850
I guess.

130
00:09:10,851 --> 00:09:12,060
You're late.

131
00:09:14,312 --> 00:09:15,772
What do you mean?

132
00:09:15,856 --> 00:09:18,108
What do you mean, what do I mean?
You're late for dinner.

133
00:09:18,191 --> 00:09:19,901
Yes, we are. We're late for dinner.

134
00:09:19,985 --> 00:09:21,570
- By a single minute.
- Yes, we were just...

135
00:09:21,653 --> 00:09:24,322
I had to put some aloe iodine
on my shoulder and...

136
00:09:24,406 --> 00:09:25,782
Just had to do his shoulder and...

137
00:09:25,866 --> 00:09:27,659
Why is there breakfast cereal
on the dinner table?

138
00:09:27,742 --> 00:09:29,035
Why are you being weird?

139
00:09:29,578 --> 00:09:32,080
- We're not being weird.
- We're not acting weird.

140
00:09:32,163 --> 00:09:34,124
Well, you're doing that weird thing
with your face.

141
00:09:34,207 --> 00:09:36,084
Well, we don't know
what you're talking about.

142
00:09:39,004 --> 00:09:40,005
Are you pregnant?

143
00:09:45,719 --> 00:09:47,637
- Yeah, we're pregnant.
- Yes, yes.

144
00:09:47,721 --> 00:09:48,722
How did you know that?

145
00:09:48,805 --> 00:09:50,557
- Have you looked at your husband's face?
- I know.

146
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:52,017
He just cannot keep a secret.

147
00:09:52,100 --> 00:09:54,144
- Wait, what? Really?
- Yeah.

148
00:09:57,230 --> 00:09:58,398
What?

149
00:09:58,481 --> 00:10:02,485
You are gonna be the best mom. Oh, my God.

150
00:10:02,569 --> 00:10:04,404
And you are gonna be the best dad.

151
00:10:04,487 --> 00:10:06,698
Just kidding. You are out of your depth.

152
00:10:06,781 --> 00:10:09,409
But we... we're gonna be
the best uncles ever.

153
00:10:10,869 --> 00:10:12,787
- Okay, we should eat.
- Okay.

154
00:10:14,122 --> 00:10:15,832
You're handling this well, you know.

155
00:10:15,916 --> 00:10:18,960
I figured you'd be locked in your lab
drenched in a panic sweat.

156
00:10:19,628 --> 00:10:21,087
I have that scheduled for later.

157
00:10:22,088 --> 00:10:23,882
{\an8}Countdown continues

158
00:10:23,965 --> 00:10:27,510
{\an8}as the Fantastic Four prepare to welcome
a new member to the family.

159
00:10:27,594 --> 00:10:32,974
<i>Needless to say, preparations inside
the Baxter Building are well underway.</i>

160
00:10:33,475 --> 00:10:36,061
All right, H.E.R.B.I.E.,
let's start the baby prep.

161
00:10:56,623 --> 00:10:57,749
H.E.R.B.I.E.!

162
00:11:03,254 --> 00:11:06,716
<i>Yancy Street bookies are putting
the odds of a girl at 4-to-5,</i>

163
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:08,760
<i>but chances of twins are a long shot.</i>

164
00:11:14,849 --> 00:11:15,850
Herbert!

165
00:11:26,319 --> 00:11:27,529
H.E.R.B.I.E.!

166
00:11:28,154 --> 00:11:30,573
The oil and gas cowboys
want a minute to yell at you

167
00:11:30,657 --> 00:11:32,409
before you go on maternity leave.

168
00:11:32,492 --> 00:11:34,911
Speaking of, coal lobby.

169
00:11:35,620 --> 00:11:36,955
Lynne, when you see Sue...

170
00:11:37,038 --> 00:11:39,124
Larry, I will tell her when I see her.

171
00:11:39,207 --> 00:11:40,250
Thank you, Lynne.

172
00:11:40,333 --> 00:11:42,377
{\an8}The question on everybody's mind is,

173
00:11:42,460 --> 00:11:45,338
{\an8}"Will the baby be born with superpowers?"

174
00:11:46,589 --> 00:11:47,924
H.E.R.B.I.E., we need to scan the baby.

175
00:11:48,008 --> 00:11:52,846
The Interna-Scan hasn't achieved the right
level of precession for clear imaging.

176
00:11:54,848 --> 00:11:56,641
New deep space transmission?

177
00:11:57,225 --> 00:11:59,436
Let's identify its origin.

178
00:11:59,519 --> 00:12:01,479
Shall we record and file it?

179
00:12:08,028 --> 00:12:10,613
2:15? What 2:15?
I don't have any meetings today.

180
00:12:11,865 --> 00:12:12,699
Reed.

181
00:12:12,782 --> 00:12:15,910
- Oh, that 2:15.
- Thank you for making the time.

182
00:12:15,994 --> 00:12:17,328
Johnny, do we have to today?

183
00:12:17,412 --> 00:12:19,539
I had some thoughts
on the new suit design.

184
00:12:19,622 --> 00:12:21,416
There are no new suit designs.

185
00:12:21,499 --> 00:12:24,919
You finished them years ago.
They have dust on them.

186
00:12:27,297 --> 00:12:29,215
I get it. You're gonna be a father soon.

187
00:12:29,299 --> 00:12:30,425
New responsibilities.

188
00:12:30,508 --> 00:12:33,303
- You're a bit scared.
- I'm not scared. I'm busy, Johnny.

189
00:12:33,386 --> 00:12:35,180
I'm busy. I'm busy.

190
00:12:35,263 --> 00:12:37,015
There's a difference.

191
00:12:41,311 --> 00:12:42,979
New transmission today.

192
00:12:44,105 --> 00:12:45,106
Have you listened to it yet?

193
00:12:45,190 --> 00:12:47,358
More of the same. It's a complex signal.

194
00:12:50,570 --> 00:12:52,030
Knock yourself out.

195
00:12:54,032 --> 00:12:56,159
Johnny, I'm running a test.

196
00:12:56,910 --> 00:12:58,203
Cool.

197
00:13:00,497 --> 00:13:01,748
I got time.

198
00:13:03,041 --> 00:13:04,876
Bridge teleportation test.

199
00:13:07,087 --> 00:13:10,173
Movement of organic matter, six meters.

200
00:13:12,133 --> 00:13:14,385
- <i>Glasses.</i>
- Thank you, Herbert.

201
00:13:15,261 --> 00:13:16,262
<i>Sparky.</i>

202
00:13:16,888 --> 00:13:18,098
Let's run it.

203
00:13:25,897 --> 00:13:26,898
It worked.

204
00:13:30,693 --> 00:13:32,445
- Johnny.
- Yep?

205
00:13:33,905 --> 00:13:35,115
Could you reset the breaker?

206
00:13:40,787 --> 00:13:41,788
Other way.

207
00:14:16,322 --> 00:14:17,323
Babe?

208
00:14:19,033 --> 00:14:20,535
Babe, when you're done, can you...

209
00:14:23,663 --> 00:14:24,831
Hello, H.E.R.B.I.E.

210
00:14:28,209 --> 00:14:29,252
<i>I</i>...

211
00:14:29,335 --> 00:14:31,087
I just went by the nursery.

212
00:14:32,881 --> 00:14:33,965
How's it looking?

213
00:14:35,091 --> 00:14:37,927
It's looking like
H.E.R.B.I.E.'s building the crib.

214
00:14:38,011 --> 00:14:40,013
Which I kinda thought was a you deal.

215
00:14:40,555 --> 00:14:41,806
I built this instead.

216
00:14:42,348 --> 00:14:44,976
Anyone can build a crib.
Only I can build this.

217
00:14:45,059 --> 00:14:48,354
Anyone can build a crib,
but not ours. Not for him.

218
00:14:48,438 --> 00:14:49,647
This is for him.

219
00:14:52,150 --> 00:14:55,612
Because unlike anyone else, his parents
have cosmically compromised DNA.

220
00:14:55,695 --> 00:14:56,696
Reed.

221
00:14:56,779 --> 00:14:59,199
Reed, we have done every test.

222
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:01,743
Well, not this one.

223
00:15:04,120 --> 00:15:05,163
You wanna see?

224
00:15:06,748 --> 00:15:07,749
Fine.

225
00:15:08,917 --> 00:15:09,959
Let's see.

226
00:15:34,901 --> 00:15:37,779
See? There's nothing wrong with him.

227
00:15:39,030 --> 00:15:41,032
He's absolutely perfect.

228
00:15:47,747 --> 00:15:49,999
That is such a bullshit way
to win an argument.

229
00:15:52,627 --> 00:15:54,462
- Happy Halloween.
- Happy Halloween.

230
00:15:54,545 --> 00:15:55,630
Easy with the candy.

231
00:15:56,506 --> 00:15:57,507
- Hi, Ben.
- Hi, Heather.

232
00:15:58,383 --> 00:16:00,134
Hey, Ben. How's Sue doing?

233
00:16:00,218 --> 00:16:02,762
Yeah, she's getting close.
She was craving some Maisie's cookies.

234
00:16:02,845 --> 00:16:05,431
Hey! What time is it? Say the thing.

235
00:16:05,515 --> 00:16:07,517
That's not really something I say.

236
00:16:07,600 --> 00:16:10,061
It's clobberin' time!

237
00:16:10,144 --> 00:16:12,313
It's just in the cartoon. Sorry, sir.

238
00:16:12,397 --> 00:16:13,815
Oh, my God. There he is!

239
00:16:13,898 --> 00:16:15,316
Hey! Lift the car!

240
00:16:15,400 --> 00:16:16,484
- Lift it!
- You want me to lift up a car?

241
00:16:16,567 --> 00:16:18,569
- This car? Right here?
- Lift the car! Lift the car!

242
00:16:18,653 --> 00:16:20,405
You guys are gonna get me in trouble.

243
00:16:20,488 --> 00:16:21,948
I'll... I'll try.

244
00:16:27,620 --> 00:16:28,496
Can't do it.

245
00:16:28,579 --> 00:16:30,999
- Come on. You can do it!
- All right. I'll try one more time.

246
00:16:33,042 --> 00:16:37,005
Lift the car! Lift the car!
Lift the car! Lift the...

247
00:16:41,426 --> 00:16:43,386
Throw the car! Throw it.

248
00:16:43,469 --> 00:16:45,638
- Throw the car? All right.
- Yeah, throw the car.

249
00:16:49,183 --> 00:16:51,644
Okay, everyone. Settle down.
Back to your game.

250
00:16:52,937 --> 00:16:55,440
Hey, maybe throw it next time.
That'll show 'em.

251
00:16:55,523 --> 00:16:58,359
No, no, no. It's okay. I love kids.

252
00:16:58,443 --> 00:17:00,361
Spend the day with ten fourth-grade girls

253
00:17:00,445 --> 00:17:01,863
and you may begin to rethink that.

254
00:17:03,197 --> 00:17:04,741
Rachel Rozman.

255
00:17:05,491 --> 00:17:06,659
- I'm Ben.
- I know.

256
00:17:06,743 --> 00:17:08,661
You grew up near on Yancy, yeah?

257
00:17:10,371 --> 00:17:11,622
Right there.

258
00:17:12,123 --> 00:17:13,207
Very near.

259
00:17:13,291 --> 00:17:15,460
You know,
it feels really good being back here.

260
00:17:15,543 --> 00:17:17,837
I like that everything stays the same.

261
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:20,506
Like Maisie's? The best.

262
00:17:20,590 --> 00:17:24,093
The black-and-white cookies were always
my favorite when I was a kid, but...

263
00:17:24,594 --> 00:17:25,845
we used to steal 'em back then.

264
00:17:28,806 --> 00:17:32,268
Okay. Well, maybe step inside next time.

265
00:17:32,352 --> 00:17:33,394
Kids would love to see ya.

266
00:17:33,478 --> 00:17:36,314
Yeah. Okay. I will. I'll bring cookies.

267
00:17:36,397 --> 00:17:38,316
Oh, yeah? Okay.

268
00:17:39,150 --> 00:17:41,361
Yeah, I'll bring cookies.

269
00:17:41,444 --> 00:17:42,779
All right.

270
00:17:42,862 --> 00:17:44,238
Sweet Jesus.

271
00:17:46,157 --> 00:17:48,242
It doesn't matter how long you beat it,

272
00:17:48,326 --> 00:17:50,661
you're not gonna make a meringue
if there's egg yolks.

273
00:17:50,745 --> 00:17:53,122
The real question is,
do you add some vinegar or not?

274
00:17:53,206 --> 00:17:55,583
I'm a vinegar guy. Always have been.

275
00:17:55,666 --> 00:17:58,086
Hey. Why the long face?

276
00:17:58,169 --> 00:17:59,170
What of it?

277
00:17:59,670 --> 00:18:02,632
Sounds like your 2:15
with Reed didn't go well.

278
00:18:02,715 --> 00:18:03,674
I'm sorry, pal.

279
00:18:03,758 --> 00:18:06,511
Hey, I'm fine, you know? I don't mind.
It's just...

280
00:18:06,594 --> 00:18:09,097
- I hear ya. We'll go to space again.
- Yeah, we will.

281
00:18:10,473 --> 00:18:11,474
Nice.

282
00:18:11,557 --> 00:18:13,476
<i>I'm Johnny Storm. Flame on.</i>

283
00:18:14,227 --> 00:18:16,145
<i>Flame on. Flame on. Flame...</i>

284
00:18:16,229 --> 00:18:17,438
Flame off.

285
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:20,441
Down.

286
00:18:22,068 --> 00:18:24,195
Fantastic Kitchen, down.

287
00:18:25,613 --> 00:18:26,447
Whoops.

288
00:18:26,531 --> 00:18:28,408
- Stop it.
- I finished the crib.

289
00:18:28,491 --> 00:18:30,993
Included two extras. I don't know why.

290
00:18:31,077 --> 00:18:32,078
Thank you.

291
00:18:33,204 --> 00:18:34,205
- Go time.
- No, it's okay.

292
00:18:34,288 --> 00:18:35,957
This... This is me.

293
00:18:37,125 --> 00:18:38,751
For the last few months,

294
00:18:38,835 --> 00:18:41,629
I've been tracking a small number
of criminal organizations.

295
00:18:42,380 --> 00:18:43,923
A small number, huh?

296
00:18:44,006 --> 00:18:45,007
Forty-seven of them,

297
00:18:45,091 --> 00:18:47,844
including the Puppet Master in the Bowery,

298
00:18:47,927 --> 00:18:49,679
the Wizard in Gramercy Park

299
00:18:50,221 --> 00:18:51,722
and Diablo in Washington Heights.

300
00:18:51,806 --> 00:18:53,266
You babyproofed the world.

301
00:18:53,766 --> 00:18:56,310
- It's a sweet gesture.
- It's a thorough gesture.

302
00:18:56,394 --> 00:18:58,104
But I like punching.

303
00:18:58,187 --> 00:18:59,897
- You mean "clobbering"?
- No, I mean "punching."

304
00:18:59,981 --> 00:19:01,732
- Let's eat.
- Hey, what time is it?

305
00:19:01,816 --> 00:19:03,067
It's dinnertime. Get inside.

306
00:19:03,151 --> 00:19:05,153
- You sure it's not clobberin' time?
- Stop it.

307
00:19:15,121 --> 00:19:16,205
- Johnny.
- On it.

308
00:19:49,530 --> 00:19:50,781
What the hell?

309
00:19:55,661 --> 00:19:57,330
Would you look at that?

310
00:20:06,672 --> 00:20:09,634
Stand clear. I need everybody to
remain calm and clear the area.

311
00:20:09,717 --> 00:20:10,801
Stay back. Out of the way.

312
00:20:10,885 --> 00:20:13,054
- Get back.
- Out of the way. Get back.

313
00:20:13,137 --> 00:20:14,847
<i>Breaking news from Times Square.</i>

314
00:20:14,931 --> 00:20:17,558
<i>There appears to be an object in the sky,</i>

315
00:20:17,642 --> 00:20:20,019
<i>debris raining down and some sort...</i>

316
00:20:45,920 --> 00:20:48,297
Are you the protectors of this world?

317
00:20:49,757 --> 00:20:50,758
Yes, we are.

318
00:20:52,093 --> 00:20:54,595
Your planet is now marked for death.

319
00:20:56,138 --> 00:20:59,559
Your world will be consumed
by The Devourer.

320
00:21:00,393 --> 00:21:02,812
There is nothing you can do to stop him.

321
00:21:02,895 --> 00:21:05,731
For he is a universal force.

322
00:21:06,232 --> 00:21:08,359
As essential as the stars.

323
00:21:11,654 --> 00:21:13,531
Hold your loved ones close,

324
00:21:14,991 --> 00:21:18,119
and speak the words
you've been afraid to speak.

325
00:21:19,912 --> 00:21:24,125
Use this time to rejoice and celebrate,

326
00:21:25,501 --> 00:21:27,461
for your time is short.

327
00:21:30,631 --> 00:21:32,550
I herald his beginning.

328
00:21:32,633 --> 00:21:34,552
I herald your end.

329
00:21:35,970 --> 00:21:37,346
I herald...

330
00:21:40,224 --> 00:21:42,018
Galactus.

331
00:22:28,147 --> 00:22:31,275
{\an8}<i>Scientists around the world are trying
to verify the origin</i>

332
00:22:31,359 --> 00:22:32,818
{\an8}<i>of this unknown space creature...</i>

333
00:22:32,902 --> 00:22:34,153
Are you tracking her?

334
00:22:34,236 --> 00:22:35,905
She is too fast to track, Johnny.

335
00:22:35,988 --> 00:22:38,491
She is too fast,
but I'm tracking where she's been.

336
00:22:39,033 --> 00:22:40,868
What's a Galactus? Right?

337
00:22:40,951 --> 00:22:42,495
And how do you consume a whole planet?

338
00:22:42,995 --> 00:22:48,542
Here. DA-773, a planet
in the Proxima Delphi system.

339
00:22:49,377 --> 00:22:51,545
- He ate that whole planet?
- Five planets, actually.

340
00:22:51,629 --> 00:22:54,340
Five have disappeared, that I'm aware of.

341
00:22:54,423 --> 00:22:55,966
There might be more that fit the pattern.

342
00:22:56,050 --> 00:22:57,259
And the pattern is what?

343
00:22:57,927 --> 00:22:59,595
That they've been chosen with great care.

344
00:23:00,513 --> 00:23:01,514
Targeted.

345
00:23:02,682 --> 00:23:04,183
And not just disappeared.

346
00:23:04,850 --> 00:23:05,851
Destroyed.

347
00:23:06,936 --> 00:23:09,939
Wait, you're saying
these planets disappearing,

348
00:23:10,022 --> 00:23:11,691
that's connected to her?

349
00:23:11,774 --> 00:23:12,942
Yes.

350
00:23:13,025 --> 00:23:17,613
I've identified the herald's
energy signature and matched it to DA-773.

351
00:23:19,573 --> 00:23:20,825
She was there.

352
00:23:23,619 --> 00:23:24,745
She was at all of them.

353
00:23:25,246 --> 00:23:28,207
So you're saying this Galactus...

354
00:23:28,290 --> 00:23:30,209
Can do exactly what she says it can do.

355
00:23:32,461 --> 00:23:34,505
How long to get <i>Excelsior</i> launch-ready?

356
00:23:37,508 --> 00:23:40,010
Either we go up there
or Galactus comes here.

357
00:23:40,094 --> 00:23:42,179
I don't know, 20 hours.

358
00:23:42,263 --> 00:23:43,889
The launch window is in 16.

359
00:23:43,973 --> 00:23:46,934
- Guys... Hey, guys.
- Like I said, 16 hours.

360
00:23:47,017 --> 00:23:48,477
- I'll start the nav plot.
- Hey, guys...

361
00:23:48,561 --> 00:23:51,272
H, you wanna buzz the prep team
and I'll meet you down there?

362
00:23:52,189 --> 00:23:54,191
She spoke to me. The herald.
She spoke to me.

363
00:23:54,275 --> 00:23:57,361
She spoke to all of us, Johnny.
Galactus, devouring...

364
00:23:57,445 --> 00:24:00,781
Well, when I chased her,
she spoke to me in her language.

365
00:24:01,365 --> 00:24:02,408
What did she say?

366
00:24:02,491 --> 00:24:04,452
Well, it was in her own language.
I don't know.

367
00:24:04,535 --> 00:24:05,911
Well, what were the context clues?

368
00:24:05,995 --> 00:24:07,913
Context. Space.

369
00:24:07,997 --> 00:24:09,707
And what was the tone?

370
00:24:09,790 --> 00:24:11,125
Angry? Threatening?

371
00:24:11,208 --> 00:24:13,294
No, no, no. Not at all. It was...

372
00:24:14,587 --> 00:24:15,880
kind.

373
00:24:15,963 --> 00:24:16,922
Kind?

374
00:24:17,006 --> 00:24:18,090
Not kind. Warm.

375
00:24:18,174 --> 00:24:20,009
- Warm?
- I don't know. It was...

376
00:24:20,092 --> 00:24:21,927
She was, like, right here.

377
00:24:22,470 --> 00:24:25,890
And I was looking into her beautiful face,

378
00:24:26,474 --> 00:24:31,020
and I saw stars,
and I could see me in her face.

379
00:24:31,103 --> 00:24:33,898
She spoke to me, and it was kind of...

380
00:24:33,981 --> 00:24:34,815
Warm?

381
00:24:34,899 --> 00:24:36,776
Kind. Kind?

382
00:24:36,859 --> 00:24:38,778
No. No. I get it.

383
00:24:39,445 --> 00:24:42,531
Johnny loves space. Johnny loves women.

384
00:24:42,615 --> 00:24:44,825
Now there's a literal naked space woman,

385
00:24:45,659 --> 00:24:46,994
and Johnny thinks they had a moment.

386
00:24:47,077 --> 00:24:49,872
I doubt she was naked.
It was probably a stellar polymer.

387
00:24:49,955 --> 00:24:52,833
For the record, Ben loves
when Johnny speaks in third person.

388
00:24:54,168 --> 00:24:55,461
We need to get ready.

389
00:25:21,070 --> 00:25:25,825
Okay. So she spoke to you, yeah? And?

390
00:25:30,120 --> 00:25:31,539
There are 23 of these.

391
00:25:32,832 --> 00:25:36,043
The only repeated language
and the oldest recordings.

392
00:25:36,126 --> 00:25:39,547
Now, I don't know who they are
or what they're saying, but this...

393
00:25:42,424 --> 00:25:43,634
this is the same.

394
00:25:45,094 --> 00:25:46,178
This is her language.

395
00:25:48,722 --> 00:25:50,933
Okay. Maybe that is something.

396
00:25:53,561 --> 00:25:55,104
Reed wants to see you in the lab.

397
00:25:55,938 --> 00:25:57,314
You summoned me.

398
00:25:58,107 --> 00:25:59,525
I finally knocked it off the list.

399
00:25:59,608 --> 00:26:00,609
What?

400
00:26:01,235 --> 00:26:02,403
The new space suits.

401
00:26:04,989 --> 00:26:06,657
It's flame-retardant.

402
00:26:06,740 --> 00:26:08,742
Maxed out oxygen supply, but...

403
00:26:08,826 --> 00:26:10,286
You have to monitor the gauge.

404
00:26:10,369 --> 00:26:12,079
If you stay flamed on in zero atmosphere,

405
00:26:12,162 --> 00:26:14,582
you will burn through your air reserves
in less than ten minutes.

406
00:26:17,251 --> 00:26:21,463
I take back every single bad thing
I've been saying about you.

407
00:26:23,090 --> 00:26:24,300
To myself.

408
00:26:25,509 --> 00:26:26,510
In private.

409
00:26:30,472 --> 00:26:32,141
Four years ago,

410
00:26:33,017 --> 00:26:34,268
we were dreamers.

411
00:26:35,978 --> 00:26:38,480
<i>Back then, the unknown meant adventure,</i>

412
00:26:40,107 --> 00:26:42,776
<i>and mystery, and discovery.</i>

413
00:26:45,195 --> 00:26:49,033
<i>With space, the greatest mystery of all.</i>

414
00:26:49,116 --> 00:26:51,785
<i>The last occasion led to the accident
that mutated them</i>

415
00:26:51,869 --> 00:26:53,329
<i>and gave them those fan...</i>

416
00:27:01,086 --> 00:27:05,466
<i>What we learned was that
the unknown also meant fear.</i>

417
00:27:07,301 --> 00:27:10,804
<i>And profound, radical change.</i>

418
00:27:20,064 --> 00:27:21,357
Hiya, pal.

419
00:27:21,440 --> 00:27:23,442
Johnny showed me the new suit.

420
00:27:23,525 --> 00:27:26,612
It's pretty spiffy,
especially compared to the old ones.

421
00:27:26,695 --> 00:27:27,988
Well, the old ones...

422
00:27:30,407 --> 00:27:31,909
weren't adequate.

423
00:27:31,992 --> 00:27:33,285
Who could've known?

424
00:27:33,911 --> 00:27:34,995
Me.

425
00:27:36,413 --> 00:27:37,665
- I could've known.
- Stop.

426
00:27:38,540 --> 00:27:41,752
Please. You gotta stop
beating yourself up about this.

427
00:27:43,420 --> 00:27:44,463
You know, Stretch,

428
00:27:45,422 --> 00:27:46,757
I got bad news for you.

429
00:27:47,758 --> 00:27:49,218
You ain't that smart.

430
00:27:49,301 --> 00:27:50,803
Except I am that smart.

431
00:27:50,886 --> 00:27:52,471
Oh, yeah? Can you cook?

432
00:27:53,180 --> 00:27:55,099
It's more of an art, not a science.

433
00:27:55,182 --> 00:27:58,227
- Did you pass your driver's test?
- That was due to poorly marked signage.

434
00:28:01,855 --> 00:28:07,319
This Galactus, this herald,
they got no idea what they're up against.

435
00:28:09,405 --> 00:28:12,783
So the four of us will return to space
and face the danger waiting there,

436
00:28:14,493 --> 00:28:17,037
<i>and we will find this Galactus.</i>

437
00:28:17,621 --> 00:28:20,040
<i>The second the engines fire,
everything you do from then on</i>

438
00:28:20,124 --> 00:28:23,877
will be the first time a pregnant woman
has done them in the history of the world.

439
00:28:25,212 --> 00:28:26,213
I know.

440
00:28:28,590 --> 00:28:29,883
I really do.

441
00:28:32,011 --> 00:28:35,597
And just because I'm not talking about it
doesn't mean I'm not thinking about it.

442
00:28:38,142 --> 00:28:39,226
About him.

443
00:28:43,647 --> 00:28:45,691
I really love my new suit.

444
00:28:45,774 --> 00:28:48,152
It's really your old one,
it's just a lot bigger.

445
00:28:50,112 --> 00:28:51,196
Bluer.

446
00:28:51,280 --> 00:28:55,242
It is actually bluer. Just a little extra
around the sides is all.

447
00:28:55,325 --> 00:28:57,411
<i>This is </i>Excelsior <i>Launch Control.</i>

448
00:28:57,494 --> 00:29:00,456
<i>T-minus two hours, 37 minutes, 20 seconds.</i>

449
00:29:01,415 --> 00:29:05,961
<i>Here we stand prepared
to face a danger that is unknown.</i>

450
00:29:11,675 --> 00:29:13,802
<i>A danger that has threatened our home,</i>

451
00:29:15,345 --> 00:29:16,805
<i>threatened our families</i>

452
00:29:18,557 --> 00:29:20,559
<i>and threatened this planet.</i>

453
00:29:24,438 --> 00:29:28,942
<i>The unknown will become known,
and we will protect you.</i>

454
00:29:29,985 --> 00:29:31,528
We will protect you.

455
00:29:47,920 --> 00:29:49,588
Final check and check, please.

456
00:29:50,547 --> 00:29:52,257
- Check.
- Check.

457
00:29:52,341 --> 00:29:53,801
Check.

458
00:29:53,884 --> 00:29:56,553
<i>Twelve, eleven,</i>

459
00:29:57,429 --> 00:30:02,976
<i>ten, nine, eight, seven...</i>

460
00:30:03,060 --> 00:30:04,478
Starting ignition sequence.

461
00:30:04,561 --> 00:30:09,358
<i>...six, five, four, three...</i>

462
00:30:09,441 --> 00:30:10,651
Go for launch.

463
00:30:10,734 --> 00:30:13,278
<i>...two, one.</i>

464
00:30:29,753 --> 00:30:31,713
The Excelsior<i> has liftoff.</i>

465
00:30:54,903 --> 00:30:59,074
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,
we have a successful launch.</i>

466
00:31:03,537 --> 00:31:07,499
<i>And from all of us on Earth,
we wish you good luck.</i>

467
00:31:08,167 --> 00:31:09,334
<i>And Godspeed.</i>

468
00:31:11,044 --> 00:31:12,171
Thank you, Earth.

469
00:31:18,343 --> 00:31:19,553
You seeing that?

470
00:31:23,265 --> 00:31:25,100
Approaching the FTL engine.

471
00:31:40,032 --> 00:31:41,283
Wait for my signal, Sue.

472
00:31:41,366 --> 00:31:42,367
Yeah.

473
00:31:42,451 --> 00:31:45,621
And three, two, one. Mark.

474
00:31:54,796 --> 00:31:58,717
And we are locked.

475
00:32:00,052 --> 00:32:02,346
And clear for FTL navigation.

476
00:32:02,429 --> 00:32:06,683
Faster-than-light in three, two, one.

477
00:32:18,528 --> 00:32:22,741
So the herald's energy signature tracks
to this binary system here.

478
00:32:23,242 --> 00:32:25,869
LHS-275, yes.

479
00:32:26,370 --> 00:32:28,872
Where we find her, we find Galactus.

480
00:32:28,956 --> 00:32:30,791
Reed, what are we up against here?

481
00:32:30,874 --> 00:32:34,127
- Some sort of a space dragon or something?
- Cool.

482
00:32:34,211 --> 00:32:36,421
We don't know.
But it's basic tactical science.

483
00:32:36,505 --> 00:32:38,382
Observe, assess capabilities,

484
00:32:38,465 --> 00:32:41,927
have H.E.R.B.I.E. collect any liquid,
gas, solid materials,

485
00:32:42,010 --> 00:32:43,387
analyze his physiology.

486
00:32:45,681 --> 00:32:49,268
Look, if he's just some big guy in a ship,
then yes, you can punch him out.

487
00:33:00,445 --> 00:33:02,698
Coming in on the dark side
of the system's larger planet.

488
00:33:02,781 --> 00:33:05,033
Copy that. I'm gonna take us out of FTL.

489
00:33:05,117 --> 00:33:07,035
Okay, everyone. Be prepared.

490
00:33:13,834 --> 00:33:15,252
So, where's this Galactus?

491
00:33:20,090 --> 00:33:21,300
That's strange.

492
00:33:22,092 --> 00:33:25,220
The herald's heat signature
is coming from inside the planet.

493
00:33:29,975 --> 00:33:31,893
What the hell is happening to that planet?

494
00:33:31,977 --> 00:33:33,437
Is there something alive down there?

495
00:33:44,865 --> 00:33:46,158
What is that?

496
00:33:48,910 --> 00:33:49,953
- Ben!
- I'm on it!

497
00:33:50,037 --> 00:33:51,955
Dropping us out of FTL.

498
00:33:56,460 --> 00:33:57,586
Watch out!

499
00:34:02,883 --> 00:34:03,967
Sue, hide us!

500
00:34:22,319 --> 00:34:25,113
It's all gone. The whole planet.

501
00:34:25,197 --> 00:34:27,449
And it was 13% larger than Earth.

502
00:34:33,538 --> 00:34:35,457
- Ben!
- It's not responding. I'm locked out.

503
00:34:37,751 --> 00:34:40,420
H.E.R.B.I.E.,
try to stabilize the engines.

504
00:34:42,506 --> 00:34:45,008
- What's going on?
- It's got us. It's pulling us in.

505
00:34:45,634 --> 00:34:46,760
Ben, save the engines.

506
00:34:47,928 --> 00:34:49,179
Save the engine!

507
00:35:23,380 --> 00:35:24,381
Johnny...

508
00:35:26,508 --> 00:35:27,884
your girlfriend's back.

509
00:35:39,479 --> 00:35:40,647
Hi.

510
00:35:41,273 --> 00:35:42,941
Galactus will see you.

511
00:35:43,442 --> 00:35:45,485
- I'll go.
- All of you.

512
00:35:47,612 --> 00:35:48,989
You should not have come.

513
00:36:28,987 --> 00:36:30,280
Follow.

514
00:36:31,406 --> 00:36:32,991
Scan everything and collect samples.

515
00:36:33,074 --> 00:36:34,075
Affirmative.

516
00:36:45,879 --> 00:36:47,339
What does Galactus want?

517
00:36:48,715 --> 00:36:51,426
He doesn't want. He feeds.

518
00:36:53,595 --> 00:36:55,972
How does he choose
which planets to consume?

519
00:36:56,515 --> 00:36:58,016
He does not.

520
00:36:59,851 --> 00:37:01,144
You choose.

521
00:37:02,562 --> 00:37:03,563
Yes.

522
00:37:07,359 --> 00:37:08,735
Johnny. What are you doing?

523
00:37:09,277 --> 00:37:10,654
I'm gonna charm her.

524
00:37:14,741 --> 00:37:15,951
So what did you say to me?

525
00:37:16,660 --> 00:37:18,245
When you threw me off your board?

526
00:37:19,496 --> 00:37:20,664
What did you say?

527
00:37:24,209 --> 00:37:25,752
It's a blessing.

528
00:37:26,461 --> 00:37:29,631
It means, "Die with yours."

529
00:37:31,258 --> 00:37:33,301
"Die with yours."

530
00:37:35,470 --> 00:37:36,638
Last question.

531
00:37:36,721 --> 00:37:40,267
So the surfboard, right?
Is that part of your body? Or is that...

532
00:37:48,984 --> 00:37:50,318
So she dumped you already?

533
00:37:50,402 --> 00:37:51,486
No. It went well.

534
00:38:07,294 --> 00:38:09,754
You stand before Galactus.

535
00:38:18,430 --> 00:38:21,266
The Devourer of Worlds honors you.

536
00:38:31,818 --> 00:38:33,028
We are honored.

537
00:38:34,738 --> 00:38:37,949
I was once little like you.

538
00:38:38,700 --> 00:38:41,202
Billions of years ago.

539
00:38:41,995 --> 00:38:44,539
A man from another world

540
00:38:45,457 --> 00:38:50,462
before this relentless, eternal hunger.

541
00:38:54,466 --> 00:38:56,468
You have traveled far.

542
00:38:59,137 --> 00:39:00,472
Yes.

543
00:39:03,183 --> 00:39:05,810
To beg for mercy.

544
00:39:07,771 --> 00:39:09,189
To talk.

545
00:39:10,106 --> 00:39:13,777
You carry the power to save your world.

546
00:39:13,860 --> 00:39:15,278
Yes. I believe we do.

547
00:39:16,112 --> 00:39:17,614
Inside her.

548
00:39:18,865 --> 00:39:20,241
The child.

549
00:39:22,869 --> 00:39:24,037
- What the hell?
- What...

550
00:39:24,579 --> 00:39:26,414
He hungers.

551
00:39:26,498 --> 00:39:27,916
What does that mean?

552
00:39:27,999 --> 00:39:30,585
I will spare your world.

553
00:39:31,461 --> 00:39:33,254
In exchange for the boy.

554
00:39:33,338 --> 00:39:35,674
What? No.

555
00:39:36,216 --> 00:39:39,094
He possesses the Power Cosmic,

556
00:39:39,177 --> 00:39:42,472
and he will inherit this cursed throne.

557
00:39:43,431 --> 00:39:46,101
It's not true. He's normal.

558
00:39:46,184 --> 00:39:49,354
We would know.
I would know. I tested the child.

559
00:39:49,437 --> 00:39:52,482
- He hides his nature from you.
- No.

560
00:40:03,493 --> 00:40:04,744
What are you doing to her?

561
00:40:05,787 --> 00:40:06,871
Baby's coming. The baby's coming.

562
00:40:06,955 --> 00:40:08,164
- Now?
- Yeah.

563
00:40:08,248 --> 00:40:10,208
You will not have our planet.

564
00:40:10,917 --> 00:40:12,794
And you will never have our son!

565
00:40:21,886 --> 00:40:24,556
I will eat your planet slowly

566
00:40:25,682 --> 00:40:28,393
while your child watches.

567
00:40:54,836 --> 00:40:55,962
No you don't!

568
00:41:06,598 --> 00:41:07,807
I'm coming, buddy!

569
00:41:09,976 --> 00:41:11,102
Go, go, go, go!

570
00:41:12,103 --> 00:41:14,689
H.E.R.B.I.E., prep all systems
for immediate launch.

571
00:41:20,820 --> 00:41:21,821
No!

572
00:41:30,914 --> 00:41:31,998
No!

573
00:41:36,419 --> 00:41:39,130
Surfboard, not part of the body.

574
00:41:48,723 --> 00:41:50,225
Come on.

575
00:42:03,613 --> 00:42:04,697
H.E.R.B.I.E.!

576
00:42:04,781 --> 00:42:06,074
Come on.

577
00:42:08,910 --> 00:42:10,119
Get us out of here, Ben!

578
00:42:10,203 --> 00:42:12,038
Hang in there, Suze, I'll get you home.

579
00:42:28,054 --> 00:42:29,264
Get us to the FTL!

580
00:42:30,765 --> 00:42:32,100
FTL in visual range.

581
00:42:33,351 --> 00:42:34,686
- Babe.
- I'm here, Sue. I'm here.

582
00:42:36,855 --> 00:42:38,314
{\an8}Surfer on our six.

583
00:42:39,732 --> 00:42:40,650
Attach then jump.

584
00:42:40,733 --> 00:42:43,278
- And go where?
- Anywhere! Just jump!

585
00:42:47,407 --> 00:42:49,492
H.E.R.B.I.E., I'm gonna need your help
stabilizing this thing.

586
00:43:00,169 --> 00:43:01,880
Hold on!

587
00:43:12,140 --> 00:43:14,392
Ben!

588
00:43:22,358 --> 00:43:24,152
We lost her. All clear.

589
00:43:31,284 --> 00:43:32,452
She's still on us.

590
00:43:32,535 --> 00:43:33,536
Johnny, kill her.

591
00:43:34,078 --> 00:43:36,372
- Really?
- Yeah. She wants to take your nephew.

592
00:43:36,456 --> 00:43:38,416
- Kill her!
- All right. All right.

593
00:43:40,585 --> 00:43:44,172
Just when I finally met
someone interesting.

594
00:43:53,640 --> 00:43:55,266
It's bending the beam!

595
00:43:55,350 --> 00:43:57,685
The wormhole is bending the beam!

596
00:44:03,149 --> 00:44:05,443
Reed, I can't get a lock on her!

597
00:44:05,526 --> 00:44:07,111
All right. Figure it out. Come on.

598
00:44:07,195 --> 00:44:08,404
Reed, what's the plan?

599
00:44:17,246 --> 00:44:18,831
Johnny, quit screwing around.

600
00:44:18,915 --> 00:44:22,001
Do I tell you how to drive the ship?
Don't tell me how to kill sexy aliens!

601
00:44:22,085 --> 00:44:23,503
Stop calling her sexy.

602
00:44:28,800 --> 00:44:30,218
Yes! Yes!

603
00:44:30,301 --> 00:44:31,594
- Yes!
- Yes!

604
00:44:37,350 --> 00:44:38,309
She's back!

605
00:44:38,393 --> 00:44:40,353
- Reed, I can't shake her.
- Working on it!

606
00:44:42,021 --> 00:44:43,940
- She's slippery!
- Reed!

607
00:44:47,944 --> 00:44:49,612
Drop us out of FTL here.

608
00:44:50,279 --> 00:44:51,990
That's a pretty big neutron star.

609
00:44:52,073 --> 00:44:54,242
I know. We're gonna use it.

610
00:44:54,325 --> 00:44:57,286
Isn't that basically a black hole?
Won't that kill us?

611
00:44:57,370 --> 00:44:58,496
Taking us out.

612
00:45:18,141 --> 00:45:19,225
What's the plan?

613
00:45:19,308 --> 00:45:22,395
Draw her close enough to the star,
she'll get stuck in the gravity well.

614
00:45:22,478 --> 00:45:23,938
There'll be a time dilation.

615
00:45:24,022 --> 00:45:26,607
- How much of a dilation?
- Is it more than mine?

616
00:45:26,691 --> 00:45:28,443
It'll take her a month to break free.

617
00:45:29,694 --> 00:45:30,862
Take us in, Ben.

618
00:45:30,945 --> 00:45:32,613
Reed, we could get sucked in.

619
00:45:33,239 --> 00:45:34,365
Ben, trust me.

620
00:45:35,033 --> 00:45:36,284
Hang on.

621
00:45:50,506 --> 00:45:51,591
Come on.

622
00:45:51,674 --> 00:45:52,633
It's chewing us up!

623
00:45:53,843 --> 00:45:54,927
Get closer.

624
00:45:55,011 --> 00:45:56,262
It's chewing us up!

625
00:45:56,345 --> 00:45:57,972
A little closer!

626
00:45:58,806 --> 00:46:00,183
Come on, Reed. What are we doing?

627
00:46:00,266 --> 00:46:03,895
Sue, we need 30 seconds of invisibility.
Can you do it?

628
00:46:04,437 --> 00:46:05,730
After your next contraction.

629
00:46:54,153 --> 00:46:55,738
- Yes!
- Hell, yeah!

630
00:46:55,822 --> 00:46:57,406
You all right, Sue?

631
00:47:00,284 --> 00:47:01,744
We need to strap you down.

632
00:47:01,828 --> 00:47:04,247
- Strapping her down.
- Do not strap me down!

633
00:47:05,248 --> 00:47:06,791
Not strapping her down.

634
00:47:08,126 --> 00:47:10,211
Baby, you need gravity to push.

635
00:47:10,878 --> 00:47:12,839
This is not right.
It's not how it's supposed to be.

636
00:47:12,922 --> 00:47:14,006
I know, I know.

637
00:47:14,090 --> 00:47:15,716
But we're gonna make it work.

638
00:47:17,218 --> 00:47:18,761
You're doing wonderful, my love.

639
00:47:22,140 --> 00:47:24,142
We don't have enough juice to get home.

640
00:47:24,225 --> 00:47:25,560
Oh, no.

641
00:47:29,313 --> 00:47:30,356
No, we do not.

642
00:47:30,439 --> 00:47:33,860
I can slingshot around the star,
draft off its orbital momentum.

643
00:47:33,943 --> 00:47:36,362
We need to get to .88 speed of light.

644
00:47:36,445 --> 00:47:38,072
Reed!

645
00:47:38,156 --> 00:47:39,782
- Johnny, the velocity gauge.
- Reed!

646
00:47:39,866 --> 00:47:40,867
On it.

647
00:47:42,410 --> 00:47:43,578
- I'm here.
- Don't go. Don't go.

648
00:47:43,661 --> 00:47:45,204
I'm not going anywhere.

649
00:47:45,288 --> 00:47:46,914
I'm right here.

650
00:47:46,998 --> 00:47:49,000
Beginning slingshot. Here we go.

651
00:47:51,878 --> 00:47:53,254
Coming up on .82.

652
00:47:53,337 --> 00:47:54,463
On your mark, Johnny.

653
00:47:56,257 --> 00:47:58,843
Why... Why do they wanna take him?
Something is wrong with him.

654
00:47:58,926 --> 00:48:00,386
- There's nothing wrong with him.
- You don't know that.

655
00:48:00,469 --> 00:48:01,596
- I do. I do know.
- No, you don't.

656
00:48:01,679 --> 00:48:03,222
You know everything,
but you don't know that.

657
00:48:03,306 --> 00:48:05,224
- What if he's a monster?
- He's not a monster.

658
00:48:06,058 --> 00:48:08,102
- Everything's gonna change.
- Nothing is gonna change.

659
00:48:08,186 --> 00:48:09,812
- Everything's gonna change.
- I promise you.

660
00:48:09,896 --> 00:48:11,564
- I promise.
- You can't promise that.

661
00:48:11,647 --> 00:48:13,107
- I promise.
- You can't promise that.

662
00:48:13,191 --> 00:48:14,525
- Reed...
- Okay.

663
00:48:18,946 --> 00:48:20,740
He's coming. He's coming.

664
00:48:20,823 --> 00:48:21,908
Give me your hand.

665
00:48:21,991 --> 00:48:23,117
.84. Ben!

666
00:48:23,201 --> 00:48:24,535
Come on!

667
00:48:27,205 --> 00:48:28,789
- Sue. Push.
- No.

668
00:48:28,873 --> 00:48:30,458
- Yes, you can.
- .85.

669
00:48:30,541 --> 00:48:31,626
- Ready?
- Okay.

670
00:48:31,709 --> 00:48:34,253
One, two, three, push!

671
00:48:38,633 --> 00:48:40,218
- Come on!
- .86!

672
00:48:40,301 --> 00:48:42,553
Push. Push. That's good.

673
00:48:44,055 --> 00:48:45,097
.87.

674
00:48:48,684 --> 00:48:50,186
- Mark!
- Ben!

675
00:48:50,269 --> 00:48:51,437
H.E.R.B.I.E.

676
00:48:53,481 --> 00:48:54,523
Ben, help!

677
00:48:55,566 --> 00:48:56,984
Thrusters engaged.

678
00:48:58,486 --> 00:48:59,904
H.E.R.B.I.E., get ready!

679
00:49:05,993 --> 00:49:07,370
Hold on, everyone.

680
00:49:33,437 --> 00:49:34,981
I got you, little guy.

681
00:50:05,761 --> 00:50:06,929
Franklin.

682
00:51:09,784 --> 00:51:12,661
{\an8}<i>After a monthlong return trip,
the Fantastic Four are finally home</i>

683
00:51:12,745 --> 00:51:14,330
<i>and receiving a warm welcome.</i>

684
00:51:24,715 --> 00:51:25,925
Her baby!

685
00:51:27,301 --> 00:51:29,595
Oh, my God. Unbelievable.

686
00:51:29,678 --> 00:51:32,014
- Lynne, we're going to need...
- Come this way.

687
00:51:35,518 --> 00:51:36,644
Reed! Reed!

688
00:51:36,727 --> 00:51:38,646
- Move back!
- Dr. Richards, over here!

689
00:51:38,729 --> 00:51:41,649
- Can we get a word?
- Stand back. Make a path.

690
00:51:41,732 --> 00:51:44,360
Sue! Sue!

691
00:51:48,823 --> 00:51:51,826
They're ready for you. Step up.
Just keep it brief.

692
00:51:56,622 --> 00:51:58,749
I'm sorry.
We don't have a prepared statement.

693
00:52:01,836 --> 00:52:04,004
One at a time, please. One at a time.

694
00:52:04,088 --> 00:52:05,131
Connor.

695
00:52:05,673 --> 00:52:08,884
Welcome back. Could you take us through
how you defeated Galactus?

696
00:52:10,594 --> 00:52:11,595
How we de...

697
00:52:15,015 --> 00:52:16,100
We didn't.

698
00:52:16,183 --> 00:52:18,561
Not yet. Not yet, we didn't.

699
00:52:18,644 --> 00:52:20,104
What does that mean?

700
00:52:20,187 --> 00:52:21,480
Follow up.

701
00:52:23,065 --> 00:52:24,442
What do you mean, you didn't?

702
00:52:26,485 --> 00:52:29,655
We attempted to negotiate, but Galactus...

703
00:52:33,200 --> 00:52:35,619
He asked too high a price.

704
00:52:35,703 --> 00:52:37,955
- Well, what does he want?
- What did he ask?

705
00:52:42,001 --> 00:52:43,544
He asked for our child.

706
00:52:46,046 --> 00:52:48,591
He said, "Give us your child,

707
00:52:50,634 --> 00:52:51,844
and I will spare the earth."

708
00:52:53,137 --> 00:52:55,473
We said no, obviously. We said no.

709
00:52:56,307 --> 00:52:58,309
We're gonna... We're gonna circle back

710
00:52:58,392 --> 00:52:59,727
with a more detailed statement...

711
00:52:59,810 --> 00:53:01,520
- You said no?
- What does that mean for us?

712
00:53:01,604 --> 00:53:03,522
Could giving Galactus the child save us?

713
00:53:05,274 --> 00:53:06,734
Hang on... You can't just...

714
00:53:06,817 --> 00:53:08,819
Just answer this. Answer this.

715
00:53:09,653 --> 00:53:11,363
Are we safe?

716
00:53:12,406 --> 00:53:13,949
- Are we safe?
- Yeah.

717
00:53:17,828 --> 00:53:18,913
I don't know.

718
00:53:19,830 --> 00:53:22,291
- What do you mean, you don't know?
- You don't know?

719
00:53:23,626 --> 00:53:26,921
What do you mean, you don't know?
What do you mean, you don't know?

720
00:53:42,353 --> 00:53:43,354
I'm sorry.

721
00:53:44,396 --> 00:53:45,773
I've failed you.

722
00:53:46,524 --> 00:53:49,193
I need the child.

723
00:53:49,276 --> 00:53:51,904
I must get the child.

724
00:53:53,322 --> 00:53:54,949
But he's just a baby.

725
00:54:00,996 --> 00:54:04,583
He is a being of infinite power,

726
00:54:05,376 --> 00:54:09,255
one strong enough to absorb my hunger,

727
00:54:10,422 --> 00:54:14,677
so that I may finally rest.

728
00:54:15,386 --> 00:54:17,763
- How much time do we even have?
- And what do we do when he gets here?

729
00:54:17,846 --> 00:54:19,890
What about the ship?
We blast it. Problem solved.

730
00:54:19,974 --> 00:54:22,476
You can't blast it.
Conventional weapons won't work.

731
00:54:22,560 --> 00:54:24,019
- So, we run.
- We run?

732
00:54:24,103 --> 00:54:26,063
Draw him away from Earth.
We're faster than him, right?

733
00:54:26,146 --> 00:54:28,107
- Not faster than the herald.
- Well, we got a head start.

734
00:54:28,190 --> 00:54:31,068
Yeah, but that's all we've got, and then
he could still eat the Earth anyways.

735
00:54:31,944 --> 00:54:33,153
Reed.

736
00:54:33,696 --> 00:54:35,406
You want to take us through what you have?

737
00:54:36,073 --> 00:54:38,158
- What I have?
- Yeah.

738
00:54:39,159 --> 00:54:40,661
What I have is nothing.

739
00:54:40,744 --> 00:54:42,454
Nothing. Did you say nothing?

740
00:54:42,538 --> 00:54:45,332
I analyzed the samples H.E.R.B.I.E. took
from Galactus's ship.

741
00:54:46,041 --> 00:54:49,628
All evidence suggests
he predates our universe, our reality.

742
00:54:49,712 --> 00:54:52,840
It could take ten years to understand
his composition, let alone his existence.

743
00:54:52,923 --> 00:54:54,174
You're talking about a god?

744
00:54:54,258 --> 00:54:56,802
I'm talking about something
beyond our experience.

745
00:54:57,303 --> 00:54:58,887
An unknowable life...

746
00:54:58,971 --> 00:55:01,056
who imagines Franklin as his successor,

747
00:55:01,140 --> 00:55:03,642
and possessing some kind of cosmic power.

748
00:55:03,726 --> 00:55:05,728
That can't be true.
You ran all those tests. Right?

749
00:55:05,811 --> 00:55:08,063
I have, but I don't know
what can or cannot be.

750
00:55:08,147 --> 00:55:10,274
I'm not sure how long.
I'm not sure of anything. I...

751
00:55:10,774 --> 00:55:11,859
I have nothing. I...

752
00:55:12,484 --> 00:55:13,736
I have nothing.

753
00:55:15,404 --> 00:55:17,656
If we could solve something,

754
00:55:17,740 --> 00:55:21,076
any link in the chain...

755
00:55:22,161 --> 00:55:25,372
E is the effort force, R is the lever arm
connected to the effort.

756
00:55:25,456 --> 00:55:27,875
L is the load, r is the lever arm
connected to the load.

757
00:55:27,958 --> 00:55:30,044
Archimedes. The Law of Levers.

758
00:55:30,127 --> 00:55:33,380
"Give me a lever and a place to stand
and I will move the earth."

759
00:55:34,715 --> 00:55:35,716
We need a lever.

760
00:55:35,799 --> 00:55:37,301
You wanna translate that?

761
00:55:37,384 --> 00:55:40,054
Yeah, we solve the right small problem,
we solve the big Galactus one.

762
00:55:40,137 --> 00:55:41,889
Yes. Yes.

763
00:55:41,972 --> 00:55:43,724
All right, boys, let's go look for levers.

764
00:55:43,807 --> 00:55:44,808
Yep.

765
00:55:47,978 --> 00:55:50,189
You know, you're supposed to sleep
when the baby sleeps.

766
00:55:50,689 --> 00:55:53,442
I've been, you know, reading the books.

767
00:55:54,693 --> 00:55:56,987
He thinks the baby actually sleeps.

768
00:55:59,823 --> 00:56:01,033
<i>It's a blessing.</i>

769
00:56:04,787 --> 00:56:05,788
<i>It's a blessing.</i>

770
00:56:09,208 --> 00:56:10,709
I gotta show you something.

771
00:56:10,793 --> 00:56:11,877
What do you wanna show me?

772
00:56:11,960 --> 00:56:13,754
- It's really good.
- I barely slept last night.

773
00:56:13,837 --> 00:56:14,880
I'm sorry to hear that.

774
00:56:14,963 --> 00:56:17,383
It's not like you chose this whole thing.
Being a mother, you know?

775
00:56:17,466 --> 00:56:19,927
Sit down. Good. I gotta show you.
Just trust me.

776
00:56:20,511 --> 00:56:22,012
Okay. All right.

777
00:56:22,096 --> 00:56:23,764
Johnny, it smells.

778
00:56:23,847 --> 00:56:25,683
It's pheromones. Relax. All right.

779
00:56:26,392 --> 00:56:27,851
Racking back the helmet cam.

780
00:56:34,233 --> 00:56:35,317
<i>It's a blessing.</i>

781
00:56:36,151 --> 00:56:38,654
<i>It means, "Die with yours."</i>

782
00:56:43,659 --> 00:56:46,120
I told you I'd heard that before.

783
00:56:47,663 --> 00:56:50,165
Now we have a sentence translated,

784
00:56:50,249 --> 00:56:52,835
and we can use that to figure out
what all of this means.

785
00:56:52,918 --> 00:56:54,378
I mean, Reed could build an algorithm,
and then...

786
00:56:54,461 --> 00:56:55,629
His big brain is busy.

787
00:56:55,713 --> 00:56:57,005
I'm all over this.

788
00:56:57,089 --> 00:57:01,343
A Rosetta stone to find him
an Archimedes lever.

789
00:57:02,010 --> 00:57:03,137
See?

790
00:57:03,220 --> 00:57:04,847
I can reference old stuff too.

791
00:57:12,688 --> 00:57:14,106
There you go. Good boy.

792
00:57:33,000 --> 00:57:36,545
{\an8}<i>Fantastic Four has verified
that an unknown spacecraft</i>

793
00:57:36,628 --> 00:57:39,965
{\an8}<i>believed to be Galactus
has just passed Jupiter.</i>

794
00:57:40,048 --> 00:57:44,595
{\an8}<i>Financial institutions remain closed
as angry protestors take to...</i>

795
00:57:44,678 --> 00:57:48,640
{\an8}<i>The newly formed Galactus cult intends
to summit Mount Ev...</i>

796
00:57:49,183 --> 00:57:52,394
<i>Tempers boiled over
in Central London today,</i>

797
00:57:52,478 --> 00:57:56,064
<i>breaking out in violence,
as the whole world wonders,</i>

798
00:57:56,565 --> 00:57:58,692
<i>"What is to be our fate?"</i>

799
00:58:01,028 --> 00:58:02,488
Hey, what about us?

800
00:58:03,781 --> 00:58:05,324
We got families too.

801
00:58:06,408 --> 00:58:08,786
Guys, it's getting bad out there.

802
00:58:09,328 --> 00:58:12,498
<i>It seems to me
they have no plan for Galactus.</i>

803
00:58:12,581 --> 00:58:15,083
<i>We, as a society,
have to reckon with the idea</i>

804
00:58:15,167 --> 00:58:17,961
<i>that the Fantastic Four
could save us today,</i>

805
00:58:18,045 --> 00:58:20,047
<i>- but they choose not to?
- No.</i>

806
00:58:20,130 --> 00:58:22,132
<i>The idea is simple.</i>

807
00:58:22,216 --> 00:58:26,678
<i>Reed Richards and Sue Storm hand over
their baby and we all live.</i>

808
00:58:26,762 --> 00:58:27,679
<i>One life...</i>

809
00:58:35,813 --> 00:58:37,105
Where are you?

810
00:58:38,106 --> 00:58:40,359
Get down from your high tower.

811
00:58:42,736 --> 00:58:45,113
You're supposed to protect us!

812
00:58:45,197 --> 00:58:46,615
Give up the baby!

813
00:58:49,618 --> 00:58:52,079
- They're scared.
- Who isn't scared?

814
00:58:52,162 --> 00:58:54,915
That is scary.

815
00:58:54,998 --> 00:58:57,376
Why? They can't hurt us.

816
00:58:57,459 --> 00:58:59,294
Well, it's scary because they hate us.

817
00:58:59,378 --> 00:59:02,798
They think they might die, and they
hate us for it. And they hate Franklin.

818
00:59:04,424 --> 00:59:07,386
And they may be right because right now,
we don't have a workable plan.

819
00:59:07,469 --> 00:59:08,971
The clock is ticking.

820
00:59:09,054 --> 00:59:10,222
So their plan looks good.

821
00:59:10,305 --> 00:59:15,602
It's mathematical, it's ethical,
and it's available.

822
00:59:17,020 --> 00:59:18,313
What are you saying?

823
00:59:19,147 --> 00:59:23,193
I'm not saying anything.

824
00:59:36,331 --> 00:59:39,293
Oh, sweetheart. It's all right, buddy.

825
00:59:45,340 --> 00:59:49,344
You know Ben's wrong.
There's always people that can hurt you.

826
00:59:50,596 --> 00:59:52,681
Sue, please hear me.

827
00:59:53,640 --> 00:59:56,226
I would never give him up to Galactus.
I would never do that.

828
00:59:56,310 --> 01:00:00,731
"Mathematical? Ethical? Available?"
It was just so easy for you to say that.

829
01:00:00,814 --> 01:00:01,815
It means nothing.

830
01:00:01,899 --> 01:00:03,775
It means I know you,
I know how your brain works.

831
01:00:03,859 --> 01:00:05,485
It means you've thought about it.

832
01:00:05,569 --> 01:00:08,196
Means you've rolled it around in your head
and you've worked the problem.

833
01:00:08,280 --> 01:00:09,448
Which means nothing.

834
01:00:10,490 --> 01:00:13,619
It is my job to think terrible things
so that terrible things don't happen.

835
01:00:13,702 --> 01:00:16,455
It's not your job, Reed. That's you.

836
01:00:17,247 --> 01:00:19,750
Okay. You're right, it is me.

837
01:00:21,627 --> 01:00:28,258
I don't dream, I don't wonder, I invite
the worst possible thing into my head

838
01:00:28,342 --> 01:00:31,762
to figure out how to hurt them
before they hurt anybody else.

839
01:00:31,845 --> 01:00:36,224
And you know what? Sometimes…
sometimes you being you hurts me.

840
01:00:40,187 --> 01:00:41,313
Well, I don't mean to.

841
01:00:46,860 --> 01:00:48,236
I know. I know.

842
01:00:50,906 --> 01:00:52,282
I know.

843
01:00:53,825 --> 01:00:56,536
Listen, I am going to solve this.
I'm gonna make it right.

844
01:01:06,797 --> 01:01:10,550
We don't know what he is
or what he might become…

845
01:01:12,803 --> 01:01:15,305
but I am not giving him up.

846
01:01:37,494 --> 01:01:38,912
You're selfish.

847
01:01:46,670 --> 01:01:48,255
How can you bring him out here?

848
01:01:49,923 --> 01:01:51,717
I wanted to introduce you to someone.

849
01:01:53,677 --> 01:01:56,263
This is our son, Franklin.

850
01:01:57,264 --> 01:01:59,057
There's been a lot of talk about him.

851
01:02:04,896 --> 01:02:08,191
Most of you know me. You know my story.

852
01:02:08,275 --> 01:02:11,236
When Johnny and I were kids,
our parents were in a car crash.

853
01:02:12,529 --> 01:02:15,323
Our dad was driving and he lived,

854
01:02:16,241 --> 01:02:17,868
but our mom didn't.

855
01:02:18,410 --> 01:02:21,788
<i>I know what it's like to be part
of a family that was torn apart.</i>

856
01:02:23,040 --> 01:02:26,043
<i>Our dad, he wasn't always a great father,
but he wanted to be.</i>

857
01:02:26,126 --> 01:02:27,294
He did his best.

858
01:02:27,377 --> 01:02:30,797
He wanted us to be together
because that's what family is.

859
01:02:31,715 --> 01:02:34,551
It's about fighting for something
bigger than yourself.

860
01:02:35,260 --> 01:02:38,013
It's about connecting to something
bigger than yourself.

861
01:02:57,449 --> 01:03:00,118
It's about having something
bigger than yourself.

862
01:03:01,078 --> 01:03:05,207
And the four of us... the four of us
already do because we have you.

863
01:03:08,627 --> 01:03:10,253
You know, our mom always used to say,

864
01:03:10,337 --> 01:03:13,799
"Suzie, for you,
I would move heaven and earth."

865
01:03:15,759 --> 01:03:17,677
And we would do that for you.

866
01:03:22,140 --> 01:03:25,811
I will not sacrifice my child
for this world.

867
01:03:28,271 --> 01:03:32,067
But I will not sacrifice this world
for my child.

868
01:03:35,654 --> 01:03:37,239
We will face this together.

869
01:03:38,240 --> 01:03:39,991
We will fight this together.

870
01:03:40,492 --> 01:03:43,120
And we will defeat this together.

871
01:03:43,203 --> 01:03:44,329
As a family.

872
01:03:50,836 --> 01:03:52,712
"As a family."

873
01:03:55,715 --> 01:03:56,883
Archimedes.

874
01:03:58,635 --> 01:03:59,719
The Law of Levers.

875
01:03:59,803 --> 01:04:02,472
"Give me a lever and a place to stand
and I will move the earth."

876
01:04:02,556 --> 01:04:05,058
We are going to move heaven and earth.

877
01:04:06,768 --> 01:04:08,061
Well, just earth.

878
01:04:08,770 --> 01:04:09,771
Sue?

879
01:04:11,523 --> 01:04:12,524
You solved it.

880
01:04:12,607 --> 01:04:13,608
I did?

881
01:04:13,692 --> 01:04:16,194
Yes. We are going to move Earth

882
01:04:16,278 --> 01:04:18,947
to a place that Galactus
will never find us.

883
01:04:19,739 --> 01:04:20,615
How?

884
01:04:21,158 --> 01:04:22,993
Well, we already have the lever.

885
01:04:23,493 --> 01:04:24,661
The bridge.

886
01:04:24,744 --> 01:04:26,329
The bridge is a prototype.

887
01:04:26,413 --> 01:04:28,081
You moved an egg across the room.

888
01:04:28,165 --> 01:04:29,624
You think you can do that with a planet?

889
01:04:29,708 --> 01:04:30,917
We are out of options.

890
01:04:31,001 --> 01:04:34,087
We have to make it work.
We will make it work.

891
01:04:35,547 --> 01:04:36,882
Heaven and earth.

892
01:04:42,804 --> 01:04:45,223
<i>We interrupt this program
with a special report.</i>

893
01:04:45,307 --> 01:04:47,225
<i>And now an announcement
from Reed Richards.</i>

894
01:04:47,309 --> 01:04:51,104
As you're about to see,
we've solved the physics of teleportation.

895
01:04:56,985 --> 01:04:58,069
H.E.R.B.I.E.

896
01:05:00,447 --> 01:05:02,866
The difference between a planet
and an egg is only scale.

897
01:05:04,618 --> 01:05:05,994
<i>Starting immediately,</i>

898
01:05:06,077 --> 01:05:08,955
<i>we will create teleportation bridges
spanning the globe.</i>

899
01:05:09,039 --> 01:05:11,541
<i>They will be synchronized
and interconnected,</i>

900
01:05:11,625 --> 01:05:13,293
<i>capable of transporting our planet</i>

901
01:05:13,376 --> 01:05:17,172
<i>to a new solar system within a 2% margin
of the inhabitable zone.</i>

902
01:05:17,881 --> 01:05:20,508
<i>But more importantly, away from Galactus,</i>

903
01:05:20,592 --> 01:05:23,136
<i>where he won't be able to find us
for millions of years.</i>

904
01:05:23,220 --> 01:05:25,013
Time is not on our side.

905
01:05:25,096 --> 01:05:27,224
I'm reaching out to the world
with a list of materials

906
01:05:27,307 --> 01:05:28,391
that we need in bulk.

907
01:05:28,975 --> 01:05:31,019
Plutonium-239.

908
01:05:33,313 --> 01:05:34,481
All right, people.

909
01:05:34,564 --> 01:05:35,941
Like my old man used to say,

910
01:05:36,024 --> 01:05:38,693
"If you don't know what to do,
pick up a shovel."

911
01:05:38,777 --> 01:05:41,112
Fire it up.
We got bridges to build. Let's go.

912
01:05:46,326 --> 01:05:49,996
<i>The last 36 hours has seen
an historical mobilization</i>

913
01:05:50,080 --> 01:05:52,123
<i>of every country working together,</i>

914
01:05:52,207 --> 01:05:55,210
<i>in a way the world has never seen before.</i>

915
01:05:59,714 --> 01:06:02,968
<i>With Galactus's ship
deep within our solar system</i>

916
01:06:03,051 --> 01:06:05,637
<i>and the Fantastic Four's
Hail Mary in the balance,</i>

917
01:06:06,346 --> 01:06:08,848
<i>we are calling on every helping hand.</i>

918
01:06:08,932 --> 01:06:12,310
If you can do something well,
now you can do it for your planet.

919
01:06:20,110 --> 01:06:24,072
<i>We are getting reports
that Galactus has passed Mars.</i>

920
01:06:26,491 --> 01:06:27,659
H.E.R.B.I.E., record.

921
01:06:36,251 --> 01:06:37,544
It takes too much power.

922
01:06:38,878 --> 01:06:41,339
I only got this to work
by tripling my intake,

923
01:06:41,423 --> 01:06:43,341
which drained the New York City grid
in two seconds.

924
01:06:43,425 --> 01:06:45,635
To do this, there isn't enough
power in the world.

925
01:06:45,719 --> 01:06:47,971
I'd have to turn off
every light switch on the planet.

926
01:06:49,514 --> 01:06:50,515
For how long?

927
01:06:51,725 --> 01:06:53,977
Factoring in
we gotta keep building bridges,

928
01:06:54,060 --> 01:06:57,022
how long would we need to conserve power?

929
01:06:58,606 --> 01:07:00,025
<i>Sacrifices will be made.</i>

930
01:07:00,984 --> 01:07:03,862
We all need to conserve power
at a scale never attempted before.

931
01:07:05,113 --> 01:07:06,323
Quite right, H.E.R.B.I.E.

932
01:07:07,073 --> 01:07:08,616
All the power.

933
01:07:09,326 --> 01:07:11,619
<i>The worldwide energy curfew only works</i>

934
01:07:11,703 --> 01:07:14,080
<i>if everybody does their part
to conserve electricity.</i>

935
01:07:20,170 --> 01:07:21,379
Missed a spot.

936
01:07:21,463 --> 01:07:25,759
Yeah. Curfew fried it.
Now I look like an idiot.

937
01:07:28,053 --> 01:07:29,262
Beard could be cool.

938
01:07:30,805 --> 01:07:31,848
Seriously?

939
01:07:33,391 --> 01:07:35,268
I built this to see what you looked like.

940
01:07:36,519 --> 01:07:37,520
You see,

941
01:07:38,313 --> 01:07:41,566
most fathers want their sons
to look exactly like them,

942
01:07:42,525 --> 01:07:43,735
inside and out.

943
01:07:44,736 --> 01:07:45,779
But...

944
01:07:47,280 --> 01:07:48,782
I don't want you to be like me.

945
01:07:52,243 --> 01:07:54,621
There's something wrong with me,
always has been.

946
01:07:59,292 --> 01:08:00,752
The more I look at you,

947
01:08:02,629 --> 01:08:03,922
the less I know.

948
01:08:05,215 --> 01:08:07,384
And the less I know, the more scared I am.

949
01:08:09,761 --> 01:08:12,972
So you know what?
I'm not gonna look anymore.

950
01:08:15,892 --> 01:08:18,269
I'm gonna let you tell me who you are.

951
01:08:18,353 --> 01:08:21,189
And if you'd like to tell me now,
that would be helpful,

952
01:08:21,272 --> 01:08:24,192
especially if you're
an all-powerful space god.

953
01:08:24,275 --> 01:08:27,404
I'd like to know that sooner
rather than later, if you don't mind.

954
01:08:31,908 --> 01:08:32,909
Oh, no.

955
01:08:34,035 --> 01:08:35,120
You're busy peeing.

956
01:08:36,579 --> 01:08:37,872
You're a very good boy.

957
01:08:47,465 --> 01:08:48,675
Thanks, buddy.

958
01:08:55,181 --> 01:08:57,100
This is going to work.

959
01:08:58,893 --> 01:08:59,978
It has to.

960
01:09:32,635 --> 01:09:34,929
Yes! Yes!

961
01:09:37,807 --> 01:09:39,559
Yep, coming. Coming, coming, coming.

962
01:09:40,894 --> 01:09:44,063
Guys, I am onto something.

963
01:09:44,147 --> 01:09:45,607
Moving a planet here, Johnny.

964
01:09:45,690 --> 01:09:48,776
Yeah, Johnny. It's four. Fantastic Four.

965
01:09:48,860 --> 01:09:50,069
Let's move a planet.

966
01:09:50,153 --> 01:09:52,447
- Cool beard.
- You mean that? Thank you.

967
01:09:53,656 --> 01:09:54,741
Copy, Delhi.

968
01:09:56,242 --> 01:09:58,286
<i>Let's do this. London, stand by.</i>

969
01:09:58,369 --> 01:09:59,537
Yes, copy, London.

970
01:10:01,080 --> 01:10:02,165
Copy, Paris.

971
01:10:02,248 --> 01:10:04,834
- Lima, do you copy?
- Copy, Rome.

972
01:10:04,918 --> 01:10:07,170
- Copy, Delhi.
- Copy, Vienna.

973
01:10:07,253 --> 01:10:08,546
Copy, Prague.

974
01:10:08,630 --> 01:10:11,341
- <i>Chicago, stand by.</i>
- Copy, Chicago.

975
01:10:12,634 --> 01:10:14,010
Earth go for countdown.

976
01:10:14,969 --> 01:10:16,262
<i>Here we go, folks.</i>

977
01:10:17,347 --> 01:10:18,348
Go.

978
01:10:18,431 --> 01:10:21,392
<i>20, 19…</i>

979
01:10:22,060 --> 01:10:26,105
<i>18, 17, 16…</i>

980
01:10:27,065 --> 01:10:31,653
<i>15, 14, 13…</i>

981
01:10:32,487 --> 01:10:34,113
<i>12...</i>

982
01:10:34,197 --> 01:10:35,198
<i>11…</i>

983
01:10:35,949 --> 01:10:39,869
<i>10, 9, 8…</i>

984
01:10:39,953 --> 01:10:42,497
<i>7, 6…</i>

985
01:10:43,915 --> 01:10:45,625
- What is that?
- What's happening?

986
01:11:11,818 --> 01:11:14,404
- She's going for this bridge.
- No.

987
01:11:15,363 --> 01:11:16,656
She's coming for Franklin.

988
01:11:18,491 --> 01:11:20,577
- Oh, my God.
- Lock the building down!

989
01:11:23,246 --> 01:11:25,164
Wait. Where's Johnny?

990
01:11:55,778 --> 01:11:57,572
<i>- Shalla-Bal.
- Shalla-Bal.</i>

991
01:11:57,655 --> 01:11:58,656
<i>Shalla-Bal!</i>

992
01:12:15,688 --> 01:12:17,605
You understand these messages…

993
01:12:18,980 --> 01:12:20,897
You know my language?

994
01:12:21,688 --> 01:12:23,730
I've learned about you.

995
01:12:25,772 --> 01:12:26,772
Shalla-Bal.

996
01:12:28,645 --> 01:12:30,813
How do you know that name?

997
01:12:30,897 --> 01:12:32,899
And how did you get these?

998
01:12:34,025 --> 01:12:36,069
Die with yours.

999
01:12:36,569 --> 01:12:39,447
How? He barely has a grasp
of the English language.

1000
01:12:39,530 --> 01:12:41,866
Twenty-three transmissions,

1001
01:12:41,949 --> 01:12:43,493
all in your language,

1002
01:12:44,285 --> 01:12:46,954
trace back to the planet Zenn-La.

1003
01:12:49,082 --> 01:12:50,083
Your home.

1004
01:12:52,293 --> 01:12:54,796
They were looking for you, to thank you.

1005
01:12:56,339 --> 01:12:58,883
Once I translated one phrase,

1006
01:12:58,966 --> 01:13:03,471
I pieced together enough language
to understand a part of your history.

1007
01:13:04,514 --> 01:13:08,476
<i>You were some sort of scientist
or astronomer.</i>

1008
01:13:09,894 --> 01:13:12,814
<i>When Galactus came,
you offered to serve as his scout</i>

1009
01:13:12,897 --> 01:13:14,273
<i>if he'd spare your planet.</i>

1010
01:13:15,233 --> 01:13:16,984
<i>Was it to spare your family?</i>

1011
01:13:40,049 --> 01:13:42,301
<i>He turned you into this.</i>

1012
01:13:45,888 --> 01:13:47,265
<i>Shalla-Bal.</i>

1013
01:13:48,391 --> 01:13:52,311
Those were messages
from the one planet Galactus spared.

1014
01:13:52,395 --> 01:13:54,021
Your planet.

1015
01:13:55,940 --> 01:13:58,192
These planets weren't so lucky.

1016
01:14:01,154 --> 01:14:03,489
How many do you remember, Shalla-Bal?

1017
01:14:03,573 --> 01:14:06,367
Proxima Delphi. Saigas.

1018
01:14:07,368 --> 01:14:08,786
Do you remember Polaris?

1019
01:14:10,997 --> 01:14:13,332
They begged for mercy.

1020
01:14:15,001 --> 01:14:18,421
You brought Galactus
to all of these planets.

1021
01:14:18,504 --> 01:14:21,716
And now, you're bringing him here.

1022
01:14:21,799 --> 01:14:24,886
To my home! To my family!

1023
01:14:42,570 --> 01:14:44,697
Just trying to save my world, you know,

1024
01:14:46,032 --> 01:14:47,200
like you did.

1025
01:14:52,497 --> 01:14:54,624
So give up the child.

1026
01:14:54,707 --> 01:14:57,668
If he was older, he would do it himself.

1027
01:14:59,170 --> 01:15:00,922
Like I did.

1028
01:15:01,005 --> 01:15:02,673
So take me.

1029
01:15:04,717 --> 01:15:06,302
Take me.

1030
01:15:06,385 --> 01:15:07,512
Not the boy.

1031
01:15:09,347 --> 01:15:11,974
Let me make the sacrifice.

1032
01:15:13,184 --> 01:15:15,645
It's not yours to make.

1033
01:15:15,728 --> 01:15:17,814
Then stay and help us.

1034
01:15:18,898 --> 01:15:21,025
There is no help.

1035
01:15:22,276 --> 01:15:25,446
Take the child
and leave this doomed place.

1036
01:15:26,447 --> 01:15:29,158
Maybe you'll live long enough
to forgive yourselves.

1037
01:15:38,835 --> 01:15:41,629
- Johnny, that was incredible.
- I mean, does it even matter?

1038
01:15:41,712 --> 01:15:42,922
You saved Franklin.

1039
01:15:43,589 --> 01:15:44,757
Yes, it matters.

1040
01:15:44,841 --> 01:15:45,925
Reed?

1041
01:15:47,552 --> 01:15:48,678
We're not leaving, are we?

1042
01:15:49,762 --> 01:15:51,180
No. No, we're not.

1043
01:15:54,600 --> 01:15:55,601
We're not leaving.

1044
01:16:03,860 --> 01:16:06,362
Yeah. Same here.
You gotta give us a second.

1045
01:16:07,029 --> 01:16:08,948
Yeah, this is Johnny Storm.
Can you hear me?

1046
01:16:09,490 --> 01:16:11,826
- The line's too busy. I'm sorry, okay?
- <i>This is London.</i>

1047
01:16:11,909 --> 01:16:14,203
<i>- This is London. Do you copy?</i>
- Hold, London.

1048
01:16:14,287 --> 01:16:15,288
<i>What's going on?</i>

1049
01:16:17,790 --> 01:16:19,625
Hold, Paris. Paris, hold.

1050
01:16:19,709 --> 01:16:21,586
- The line's not very clear.
- There's an error. Hold the line.

1051
01:16:23,671 --> 01:16:26,674
Chicago, yes, we're onto it.
We're just... We're fixing the problem.

1052
01:16:31,971 --> 01:16:34,515
We're trying to get...
We're trying to get on top of this.

1053
01:16:34,599 --> 01:16:35,850
Sydney, stand by.

1054
01:16:35,933 --> 01:16:37,685
- Tokyo, stand by.
- Sir, you're going to have to be patient.

1055
01:16:37,768 --> 01:16:38,769
- Hold. Hold.
- Yeah, we're working on...

1056
01:16:38,853 --> 01:16:40,187
- We have to bring him here.
- We're fixing something.

1057
01:16:40,271 --> 01:16:41,439
We are aware.

1058
01:16:42,356 --> 01:16:44,191
Yes, I understand. Can you stand by?

1059
01:16:44,275 --> 01:16:46,611
- We are aware. I'll… I'll update you.
- Yeah.

1060
01:16:47,278 --> 01:16:48,279
Yeah. This is gonna have to...

1061
01:16:48,362 --> 01:16:50,323
We need to bring Galactus here.

1062
01:16:50,406 --> 01:16:51,908
- I will come back to you. Hold...
- You...

1063
01:16:52,575 --> 01:16:53,784
- Call you back.
- Hold up.

1064
01:16:54,327 --> 01:16:55,328
Reed.

1065
01:16:55,912 --> 01:16:57,830
We need Galactus to come here?

1066
01:16:57,914 --> 01:17:00,666
I feel like we just spent a lot of time
trying to prevent that from happening.

1067
01:17:00,750 --> 01:17:02,710
Listen to me.
We need to get him away from his ship.

1068
01:17:02,793 --> 01:17:05,755
We need to bring him here,
to Times Square.

1069
01:17:05,838 --> 01:17:06,797
And then what?

1070
01:17:06,881 --> 01:17:10,468
And then, instead of moving a planet
away from one giant...

1071
01:17:11,010 --> 01:17:13,471
{\an8}we move one giant away from the planet.

1072
01:17:13,554 --> 01:17:17,266
{\an8}If we route every power grid
on the Eastern Seaboard,

1073
01:17:17,350 --> 01:17:19,268
through our one last bridge,

1074
01:17:19,352 --> 01:17:20,853
charge back up,

1075
01:17:21,354 --> 01:17:25,107
we can keep the portal open for...

1076
01:17:34,200 --> 01:17:35,409
Thirty-seven seconds.

1077
01:17:35,493 --> 01:17:40,081
Thirty... Not a lot of time
to throw a space god off a planet.

1078
01:17:40,164 --> 01:17:42,375
- No, it is not.
- And where do we send him?

1079
01:17:42,917 --> 01:17:45,836
To the far edges of the universe.
Without a ship, he'll be stranded.

1080
01:17:45,920 --> 01:17:48,005
How are we supposed to
get Galactus to Times Square?

1081
01:17:48,089 --> 01:17:51,342
And how do we move one giant
through one large bridge?

1082
01:17:54,929 --> 01:17:56,806
I haven't figured that part out yet.

1083
01:18:00,851 --> 01:18:01,936
You have.

1084
01:18:02,895 --> 01:18:03,938
Have what?

1085
01:18:04,647 --> 01:18:06,691
We have to use the only thing
Galactus wants.

1086
01:18:06,774 --> 01:18:09,443
- No. I'll think of another way.
- What are you talking about?

1087
01:18:09,527 --> 01:18:11,153
You can't. You can't think of another way.

1088
01:18:11,237 --> 01:18:12,863
- I will.
- There is only one way.

1089
01:18:12,947 --> 01:18:14,281
What are you talking about?

1090
01:18:16,617 --> 01:18:18,285
We have to use Franklin.

1091
01:18:21,163 --> 01:18:22,164
Yes.

1092
01:18:22,748 --> 01:18:23,874
You wanna use the boy?

1093
01:18:27,628 --> 01:18:29,463
You wanna use the boy as bait.

1094
01:18:29,547 --> 01:18:31,382
- No.
- That's your plan?

1095
01:18:31,465 --> 01:18:33,426
No, it's not my plan. It's our plan.

1096
01:18:33,509 --> 01:18:35,011
It's the only plan.

1097
01:18:35,094 --> 01:18:37,096
- It's not my plan. I hate that plan.
- It's a bad plan.

1098
01:18:37,179 --> 01:18:38,556
- Come on. That's a stupid plan.
- Terrible idea.

1099
01:18:38,639 --> 01:18:42,059
Why don't I just burn through his ship?
That's another plan.

1100
01:18:42,143 --> 01:18:43,227
It's your kid we're talking about.

1101
01:18:43,310 --> 01:18:44,979
- Sue.
- There's gotta be a different way.

1102
01:18:45,062 --> 01:18:46,856
- I know.
- Sue. Sue.

1103
01:18:46,939 --> 01:18:48,733
Yes, I know. I know. I know!

1104
01:19:17,803 --> 01:19:20,931
I thought this was one of the most
beautiful things we'd ever built.

1105
01:19:23,684 --> 01:19:25,394
Feels terrifying now.

1106
01:19:26,937 --> 01:19:28,647
It can be beautiful again.

1107
01:19:30,232 --> 01:19:31,567
Everything can.

1108
01:19:42,036 --> 01:19:43,120
They've been gone a while.

1109
01:19:45,164 --> 01:19:46,165
Johnny.

1110
01:19:46,957 --> 01:19:48,250
Go check. See if they're back.

1111
01:19:48,334 --> 01:19:51,212
I'm in no rush to do that.

1112
01:19:52,004 --> 01:19:53,464
Well, I'm definitely not gonna check.

1113
01:19:53,547 --> 01:19:55,925
- I'm definitely not going either.
- Thank you for going and checking.

1114
01:19:56,008 --> 01:19:57,676
You're welcome. It's the least I could do

1115
01:19:57,760 --> 01:19:59,053
to say thank you for going down
to check first.

1116
01:19:59,136 --> 01:20:00,554
I'm definitely not going down.

1117
01:20:00,638 --> 01:20:01,555
Chickenshits.

1118
01:20:01,639 --> 01:20:02,473
Jesus.

1119
01:20:03,015 --> 01:20:03,849
Don't do that.

1120
01:20:03,933 --> 01:20:05,434
- I hate it when you do that.
- Don't do that.

1121
01:20:05,518 --> 01:20:07,937
Come on. Let's run through the details.

1122
01:20:09,772 --> 01:20:11,565
I don't like when she does that.

1123
01:20:11,649 --> 01:20:15,528
It's like... It's unsettling
when people just appear like that.

1124
01:20:17,655 --> 01:20:19,865
Bombproof. Shockproof.

1125
01:20:20,950 --> 01:20:22,243
Radiation-proof.

1126
01:20:26,247 --> 01:20:28,999
Franklin will go here
when Galactus arrives.

1127
01:20:30,126 --> 01:20:33,295
Hey, do we know what direction
Galactus will be coming from?

1128
01:20:34,672 --> 01:20:35,923
Well, it could be from anywhere.

1129
01:20:36,006 --> 01:20:39,552
But when he crosses those lines,
we trigger it.

1130
01:20:41,720 --> 01:20:43,597
We're in the very center of the city.

1131
01:20:44,306 --> 01:20:47,476
We're surrounded by
miles of apartment buildings.

1132
01:20:48,394 --> 01:20:49,395
Any path he takes,

1133
01:20:49,478 --> 01:20:52,773
he's gonna be going through
thousands and thousands of families.

1134
01:20:54,525 --> 01:20:56,235
I got an idea you'll hate.

1135
01:20:59,280 --> 01:21:01,991
Oh, my.

1136
01:21:02,074 --> 01:21:03,742
Very advanced.

1137
01:21:03,826 --> 01:21:07,955
So this must be where the sausage is made.

1138
01:21:09,331 --> 01:21:11,834
I think I prefer just trying
to steal the sausage.

1139
01:21:11,917 --> 01:21:13,294
Please, don't touch.

1140
01:21:15,963 --> 01:21:16,964
We'll fix that.

1141
01:21:18,299 --> 01:21:19,550
Harvey...

1142
01:21:19,633 --> 01:21:21,802
Hello there, little robot man.

1143
01:21:22,386 --> 01:21:24,221
Could you dim the lights for me, please?

1144
01:21:26,390 --> 01:21:29,268
Harvey, we wanted to ask you something.

1145
01:21:29,351 --> 01:21:32,980
And whatever it is,
I would like him to ask me.

1146
01:21:33,063 --> 01:21:35,774
It's not Reed or me asking.

1147
01:21:35,858 --> 01:21:37,484
It's the entire planet asking.

1148
01:21:37,568 --> 01:21:40,196
It wouldn't be the entire planet now,
would it? Just the over part.

1149
01:21:40,279 --> 01:21:43,824
No, Mr. Elder. We've met Galactus.
He'll eat the under part first.

1150
01:21:43,908 --> 01:21:48,037
Well, regardless,
why don't you butter me up?

1151
01:21:51,248 --> 01:21:52,333
Spread it on.

1152
01:21:52,416 --> 01:21:53,918
Okay, Mole Man.

1153
01:21:54,001 --> 01:21:56,253
- Mole Man? Really?
- You touch another piece of my...

1154
01:21:56,337 --> 01:21:57,213
Take the "mole" out of it.

1155
01:21:57,296 --> 01:21:58,505
- It's Mr. Elder to you.
- That is enough.

1156
01:21:58,589 --> 01:22:00,591
Give us a minute. Just give us a minute.

1157
01:22:00,674 --> 01:22:01,800
Yes, that's it.

1158
01:22:03,093 --> 01:22:05,304
Johnny, don't be mad. I didn't dress you.

1159
01:22:05,387 --> 01:22:07,306
Don't listen to him. You're handsome.

1160
01:22:08,641 --> 01:22:09,767
Harvey.

1161
01:22:09,850 --> 01:22:11,685
I'm sorry, Sue. I'm...

1162
01:22:12,519 --> 01:22:13,979
End of days.

1163
01:22:14,063 --> 01:22:16,315
We all gotta learn how to laugh.

1164
01:22:17,149 --> 01:22:18,776
So what do you need?

1165
01:22:19,693 --> 01:22:23,197
<i>Evacuation orders are in effect
in the Greater New York area.</i>

1166
01:22:23,280 --> 01:22:24,990
<i>Please report to Subterranea.</i>

1167
01:22:26,283 --> 01:22:29,536
<i>Evacuation orders are in effect
in the Greater New York area.</i>

1168
01:22:29,620 --> 01:22:31,664
<i>Please report to Subterranea.</i>

1169
01:22:38,545 --> 01:22:41,215
Welcome to Subterranea.

1170
01:22:42,132 --> 01:22:43,467
Hello there.

1171
01:22:44,093 --> 01:22:46,095
Welcome, sunshiners.

1172
01:22:46,178 --> 01:22:47,972
Thank you so much.

1173
01:22:48,514 --> 01:22:52,184
Yes, do me a favor
and just wipe your feet upon entering.

1174
01:22:52,268 --> 01:22:54,603
I'm kidding. It's all dirt.

1175
01:22:55,104 --> 01:22:56,563
Please, keep a move on.

1176
01:23:02,820 --> 01:23:04,363
<i>Good evening.</i>

1177
01:23:04,446 --> 01:23:06,282
<i>We, the people of Earth, prepare</i>

1178
01:23:06,365 --> 01:23:08,784
<i>for what could be our final moments.</i>

1179
01:23:09,868 --> 01:23:12,246
<i>The hours ahead may feel long,</i>

1180
01:23:12,746 --> 01:23:15,666
<i>but we must use them
to support each other,</i>

1181
01:23:16,500 --> 01:23:18,043
<i>and we must hope.</i>

1182
01:23:18,669 --> 01:23:19,837
<i>We must dare to hope.</i>

1183
01:23:19,920 --> 01:23:21,964
- Hey, Mrs. H.
- Thank you, Ben.

1184
01:23:24,216 --> 01:23:25,926
<i>We must use the time wisely</i>

1185
01:23:26,010 --> 01:23:27,803
<i>to be with the ones we cherish.</i>

1186
01:23:35,978 --> 01:23:37,730
Keep hope, all right?

1187
01:23:38,647 --> 01:23:39,648
What?

1188
01:23:43,569 --> 01:23:45,154
Sorry, just... Hi.

1189
01:23:45,237 --> 01:23:46,613
- Hey.
- Hey.

1190
01:23:47,906 --> 01:23:50,117
You're looking very distinguished.

1191
01:23:50,200 --> 01:23:52,036
I'm surprised to see you here. I...

1192
01:23:52,119 --> 01:23:53,912
Did you come for spiritual guidance?

1193
01:23:54,455 --> 01:23:55,831
Oh, no, no.

1194
01:23:55,914 --> 01:23:58,375
I just came to see you.

1195
01:24:09,386 --> 01:24:12,014
<i>I leave you tonight with these words.</i>

1196
01:24:13,307 --> 01:24:17,603
<i>"Never doubt that a small group
of thoughtful, committed citizens</i>

1197
01:24:17,686 --> 01:24:19,563
<i>can change the world.</i>

1198
01:24:20,481 --> 01:24:25,569
<i>Indeed, it's the only thing
that ever has."</i>

1199
01:25:14,284 --> 01:25:15,411
Positions.

1200
01:27:46,353 --> 01:27:48,855
Hey. Hey, hey, hey. Don't cry.

1201
01:27:49,898 --> 01:27:51,567
I'll be back in a minute, little guy.

1202
01:28:00,784 --> 01:28:02,244
Just a couple more steps.

1203
01:28:03,370 --> 01:28:04,454
Come on, come on.

1204
01:28:30,147 --> 01:28:31,773
Clever little bugs.

1205
01:28:34,359 --> 01:28:35,652
He's going for Franklin.

1206
01:29:03,805 --> 01:29:05,807
Light him up, Johnny.

1207
01:29:29,039 --> 01:29:30,248
Ben!

1208
01:30:05,867 --> 01:30:06,910
Oh, my God.

1209
01:31:18,064 --> 01:31:19,316
What time is it, Ben?

1210
01:31:19,399 --> 01:31:20,400
No.

1211
01:31:20,484 --> 01:31:22,903
- What time is it, Ben?
- No, Johnny.

1212
01:31:22,986 --> 01:31:24,821
- Say it!
- I don't wanna.

1213
01:31:24,905 --> 01:31:26,490
Say it!

1214
01:31:26,573 --> 01:31:29,743
It's clobberin' time!

1215
01:32:29,427 --> 01:32:32,347
You are my salvation.

1216
01:32:33,598 --> 01:32:36,643
My deliverance from this vicious hunger.

1217
01:32:39,938 --> 01:32:42,148
Time to feed.

1218
01:32:55,161 --> 01:32:56,621
Put down my son.

1219
01:33:45,295 --> 01:33:47,088
Sue. Sue, stop.

1220
01:33:48,715 --> 01:33:50,550
Sue, stop. It's too much.

1221
01:33:50,634 --> 01:33:52,385
- Get Franklin.
- Sue, stop!

1222
01:33:52,469 --> 01:33:53,595
Save our son.

1223
01:34:02,771 --> 01:34:04,522
Johnny, the controls.

1224
01:34:40,809 --> 01:34:42,143
Hang on, Suze!

1225
01:35:00,662 --> 01:35:01,830
Johnny, now!

1226
01:35:51,087 --> 01:35:53,089
Reed! It worked.

1227
01:35:54,174 --> 01:35:55,175
No!

1228
01:36:08,063 --> 01:36:10,065
Tell Franklin Uncle Johnny loves him.

1229
01:36:50,730 --> 01:36:51,731
Sue.

1230
01:36:57,695 --> 01:36:58,655
Sue?

1231
01:37:01,825 --> 01:37:03,952
No, no, no. No, no, no.

1232
01:37:07,455 --> 01:37:08,623
- I got him.
- Sue.

1233
01:37:12,836 --> 01:37:14,087
No.

1234
01:37:14,170 --> 01:37:16,047
No. Sue. Sue.

1235
01:37:18,258 --> 01:37:19,217
- She breathing?
- No.

1236
01:37:19,843 --> 01:37:21,052
No. No, baby. No.

1237
01:37:21,136 --> 01:37:23,054
You stay with us. You stay with us, okay?

1238
01:37:34,107 --> 01:37:37,569
Stay with me, Sue.
Stay with us, baby. Stay with us, baby.

1239
01:37:39,279 --> 01:37:40,113
Come on, Sue.

1240
01:37:40,196 --> 01:37:42,073
Come on, Sue, stay with us.

1241
01:37:42,157 --> 01:37:43,116
Don't leave us, baby.

1242
01:37:43,950 --> 01:37:44,826
<i>Sue!</i>

1243
01:37:46,077 --> 01:37:47,370
<i>Come on, baby!</i>

1244
01:37:58,673 --> 01:37:59,883
I'm sorry.

1245
01:40:03,756 --> 01:40:04,924
Hey.

1246
01:40:12,765 --> 01:40:14,058
He's not us.

1247
01:40:14,726 --> 01:40:15,935
He's more.

1248
01:40:48,760 --> 01:40:53,014
<i>Wow, folks. We have so much
exciting ground to cover today.</i>

1249
01:40:53,681 --> 01:40:56,267
The last year, a lot has happened.

1250
01:40:56,351 --> 01:40:57,769
We have seen it with our own eyes,

1251
01:40:57,852 --> 01:41:00,021
but tonight we're gonna
see it through theirs.

1252
01:41:00,104 --> 01:41:02,690
